287
00:12:33,291 --> 00:12:35,208
that they got your letter. Pack up your stuff, shoe-shine, get out of here!-

288
00:12:35,416 --> 00:12:36,000
Huh?

289
00:12:36,041 --> 00:12:37,500
Do you own this alley or something?-

290
00:12:37,500 --> 00:12:39,291
Get lost, you jerk!

291
00:12:39,291 --> 00:12:40,125
You hear? You're the jerk!-

292
00:12:40,250 --> 00:12:42,250
This noise and shouting... -Not once or twice, we told you a hundred times,

293
00:12:42,291 --> 00:12:43,916
what's it all about? Get out of our alley!-

294
00:12:43,958 --> 00:12:45,416
Saeed! Who are you around here to give us orders?-

295
00:12:45,458 --> 00:12:46,541
Go see what this noise is.

296
00:12:46,583 --> 00:12:48,083
Saeed! Run!

297
00:12:48,125 --> 00:12:49,208
It's our own Sir!-

298
00:12:49,208 --> 00:12:50,291
Our alley isn't auntie's house,-

299
00:12:50,291 --> 00:12:51,666
where any mama's boy who's mad at mama can-

300
00:12:51,666 --> 00:12:53,000
open a shop! Go!-

301
00:12:53,041 --> 00:12:54,333
Dear Uncle! Dear Uncle! Get up go...!-

302
00:12:54,375 --> 00:12:55,125
A shoe-shine came,

303
00:12:55,166 --> 00:12:56,666
he wants to set up his stall in front of the garden door,

304
00:12:56,666 --> 00:12:57,750
Mash Ghasem wants to turn him away!

305
00:12:57,958 --> 00:12:58,708
What?!

306
00:12:58,875 --> 00:12:59,458
Ghasem?

307
00:12:59,500 --> 00:12:59,833
Yes!

308
00:12:59,875 --> 00:13:00,791
Shoe-shine?

309
00:13:01,083 --> 00:13:04,208
How dare Ghasem!

310
00:13:04,250 --> 00:13:05,416
You brought this on yourself!-

311
00:13:06,333 --> 00:13:09,541
Hey, hey, let him go, you idiot!

312
00:13:09,583 --> 00:13:11,916
I'm not from Ghiyas-Abad if I don't make you pay!

313
00:13:11,958 --> 00:13:14,333
What the hell? Have you gone rabid?

314
00:13:14,333 --> 00:13:15,166
Sir we tell him,

315
00:13:15,166 --> 00:13:16,291
why did you set up your stall here?

316
00:13:16,333 --> 00:13:17,708
He’s picking a quarrel with us!

317
00:13:17,750 --> 00:13:19,375
Sir we came to sit here and work,

318
00:13:19,375 --> 00:13:20,458
and he's cursing us!

319
00:13:20,666 --> 00:13:21,416
Look, my man,

320
00:13:21,458 --> 00:13:22,500
can't you say it nicely?

321
00:13:22,833 --> 00:13:23,791
Well he's right.

322
00:13:23,833 --> 00:13:24,750
Fine, we're off!

323
00:13:24,875 --> 00:13:26,833
As if this alley belonged to the people of Ghiyas-Abad!

324
00:13:28,541 --> 00:13:29,166
Let go of my hand!

325
00:13:29,208 --> 00:13:30,000
If one more time,

326
00:13:30,000 --> 00:13:31,375
you say the name Ghiyas-Abad, Let go of my collar!-

327
00:13:31,375 --> 00:13:32,125
I'll punch you in the snout so hard

328
00:13:32,166 --> 00:13:33,291
your teeth hit the ground!

329
00:13:33,291 --> 00:13:34,208
Help!

330
00:13:34,916 --> 00:13:37,666
Ghasem, let him go before I strangle you! You bastard!-

331
00:13:37,958 --> 00:13:39,833
Man, what right do you have

332
00:13:39,875 --> 00:13:41,541
to stop people earning a living?

333
00:13:41,666 --> 00:13:43,458
Is he taking your bread?

334
00:13:43,500 --> 00:13:45,083
Sir, didn't you yourself order

335
00:13:45,083 --> 00:13:47,041
us to keep these riff-raff away?

336
00:13:47,041 --> 00:13:48,458
You yourself were saying,

337
00:13:48,500 --> 00:13:50,000
these people come to case the houses,

338
00:13:50,041 --> 00:13:51,375
so they can steal at night!

339
00:13:51,666 --> 00:13:52,791
Fool!

340
00:13:52,958 --> 00:13:56,083
I said suspicious people!

341
00:13:56,125 --> 00:13:56,541
Yes!-

342
00:13:56,541 --> 00:13:58,333
Not this poor tradesman,

343
00:13:58,333 --> 00:14:00,791
who just wants to earn a crust of bread!

344
00:14:00,833 --> 00:14:01,583
Sir, why lie?

345
00:14:01,625 --> 00:14:03,208
The grave is this close!

346
00:14:03,458 --> 00:14:06,041
I've never in my life seen a more suspishus man!

347
00:14:06,208 --> 00:14:07,166
His face oozes

348
00:14:07,166 --> 00:14:09,500
theft, lechery and suspishusness!

349
00:14:09,500 --> 00:14:10,416
Watch your mouth!

350
00:14:10,416 --> 00:14:11,125
I'm off!

351
00:14:11,125 --> 00:14:12,791
But it's a shame, Sir,

352
00:14:12,833 --> 00:14:14,750
that you have such an ass servant!

353
00:14:15,000 --> 00:14:16,125
Your father's the ass!

354
00:14:16,166 --> 00:14:17,666
Be calm Ghasem!

355
00:14:17,708 --> 00:14:18,458
Yes, yes!

356
00:14:18,458 --> 00:14:19,333
You too, let it go already!

357
00:14:20,375 --> 00:14:21,250
Mister shoe-shine!

358
00:14:21,541 --> 00:14:22,916
May I ask your name?

359
00:14:23,000 --> 00:14:24,375
Your servant, Houshang.

360
00:14:24,416 --> 00:14:25,208
Houshang?

361
00:14:26,500 --> 00:14:27,041
Strange!

362
00:14:27,541 --> 00:14:29,250
If he swears at me like that one more time,

363
00:14:29,250 --> 00:14:30,708
I'll kick him in the balls!

364
00:14:30,750 --> 00:14:32,041
What kind of talk is that? Enough!

365
00:14:32,250 --> 00:14:32,916
If sometime,

366
00:14:32,958 --> 00:14:35,458
you need a shine, a half-sole, a stitch job...

367
00:14:35,500 --> 00:14:36,791
I'm two alleys down.

368
00:14:36,958 --> 00:14:37,541
The arched alley.

369
00:14:37,625 --> 00:14:38,083
Right nearby.

370
00:14:38,208 --> 00:14:38,500
Down.

371
00:14:38,875 --> 00:14:40,375
No Sir! Where?

372
00:14:40,375 --> 00:14:43,083
This very alley is better than anywhere.

373
00:14:43,291 --> 00:14:44,666
From morning to evening,

374
00:14:44,708 --> 00:14:46,250
we have all kinds of polishing,

375
00:14:46,291 --> 00:14:48,500
shoe repair and that sort of work.

376
00:14:48,708 --> 00:14:51,083
If just the family gives you work,

377
00:14:51,208 --> 00:14:53,250
you won't need work from anywhere else!

378
00:14:53,291 --> 00:14:54,333
No Sir, we're going.

379
00:14:54,416 --> 00:14:57,625
A hundred pounds of game isn't worth the stink of the hound.

380
00:14:57,875 --> 00:14:58,708
Yeah, right.

381
00:14:58,750 --> 00:15:00,958
I've half a mind to show him the hound's stink!

382
00:15:01,000 --> 00:15:02,291
No. Houshang Khan.

383
00:15:02,375 --> 00:15:04,708
Please, stay right here.

384
00:15:04,791 --> 00:15:06,291
I give you my word,

385
00:15:06,375 --> 00:15:08,125
that Ghasem will treat you

386
00:15:08,125 --> 00:15:09,375
like a brother.

387
00:15:09,458 --> 00:15:10,583
Isn't that so, Ghasem?

388
00:15:11,041 --> 00:15:13,708
Do you promise to treat him exactly like a brother?

389
00:15:13,750 --> 00:15:14,375
He promises. Yes.

390
00:15:14,375 --> 00:15:15,041
Sir, why lie!

391
00:15:15,125 --> 00:15:16,791
The grave is this close!

392
00:15:17,125 --> 00:15:18,375
As you command.

393
00:15:18,791 --> 00:15:19,916
But Sir,

394
00:15:20,083 --> 00:15:22,083
have you forgotten that photographer so soon?

395
00:15:22,208 --> 00:15:24,208
That was a photographer.

396
00:15:24,416 --> 00:15:26,375
This is a shoe-shine.

397
00:15:28,208 --> 00:15:29,375
Sir, seems I

398
00:15:29,416 --> 00:15:30,208
took this shoe-shine

399
00:15:30,250 --> 00:15:32,250
for the cobbler at the little bazaar.

400
00:15:33,916 --> 00:15:35,083
Houshang Khan!

401
00:15:35,083 --> 00:15:38,208
At noon Ghasem brings lunch from the house.

402
00:15:38,708 --> 00:15:39,500
Ghasem!

403
00:15:39,541 --> 00:15:41,083
Tell Naneh Belqis,

404
00:15:41,083 --> 00:15:42,375
when the food is ready,

405
00:15:42,416 --> 00:15:45,958
to dish up a full plate for Houshang Khan,

406
00:15:46,166 --> 00:15:48,583
with bread, yogurt and fresh herbs.

407
00:15:48,625 --> 00:15:50,208
Sir, may God bless your bread.

408
00:15:50,333 --> 00:15:51,958
Choke on it! We've got bread and cheese here, we'll eat.-

409
00:15:52,041 --> 00:15:53,833
No, no, absolutely not!

410
00:15:53,875 --> 00:15:55,750
Be my guest for lunch today.

411
00:15:55,791 --> 00:15:57,875
You must come into the garden and eat.

412
00:15:57,916 --> 00:15:58,791
God reward you.

413
00:15:58,833 --> 00:16:00,375
Aren't you coming?

414
00:16:00,375 --> 00:16:01,875
I have to pop over to the bazaar.

415
00:16:01,916 --> 00:16:03,333
Thank you for your kindness. Goodbye.

416
00:16:03,666 --> 00:16:04,541
Goodbye.

417
00:16:05,125 --> 00:16:06,333
Bless you, son. Thank you-

418
00:16:11,333 --> 00:16:11,750
Son!

419
00:16:12,000 --> 00:16:13,375
I'm going to the bazaar, I have work.

420
00:16:13,458 --> 00:16:14,958
Tell your mother I'm home for lunch.

421
00:16:15,125 --> 00:16:15,458
Go, son.

422
00:16:15,500 --> 00:16:15,875
Yes.

423
00:16:16,416 --> 00:16:16,791
Run.

424
00:16:16,958 --> 00:16:19,250
Noon, sister! Mashti will be home soon-

425
00:16:19,333 --> 00:16:20,875
I think today he has a guest.-

426
00:16:21,041 --> 00:16:22,833
I still haven't made anything for them.

427
00:16:22,958 --> 00:16:24,500
Don't take these words of Mash Ghasem to heart.

428
00:16:24,541 --> 00:16:26,333
No Sir! I don't care what he says.

429
00:16:31,041 --> 00:16:32,000
(He knocks at the door)

430
00:16:45,291 --> 00:16:46,541
Come eat meat.

431
00:16:46,625 --> 00:16:47,250
Come.

432
00:16:49,041 --> 00:16:49,833
Come.

433
00:16:53,666 --> 00:16:56,375
Damn every shameless shoe-shine's donkey father!

434
00:16:56,416 --> 00:16:57,416
Eat.

435
00:17:00,666 --> 00:17:03,791
Damn you, aren't you ashamed?

436
00:17:04,333 --> 00:17:06,916
This food is that poor shoe-shine's.

437
00:17:07,000 --> 00:17:08,708
You're feeding his meat to the cat?

438
00:17:08,750 --> 00:17:09,708
No, no, no Sir!

439
00:17:09,750 --> 00:17:10,375
Am I a heathen

440
00:17:10,416 --> 00:17:12,208
that I'd give the poor creature's meat to a cat?

441
00:17:12,500 --> 00:17:15,500
Damn that ill-omened lying face of yours!

442
00:17:15,708 --> 00:17:17,125
Right now, before my eyes,

443
00:17:17,125 --> 00:17:18,666
you're feeding his meat to the cat!

444
00:17:18,791 --> 00:17:20,083
Sir, why lie!

445
00:17:20,291 --> 00:17:21,250
The grave's...

446
00:17:21,708 --> 00:17:23,791
The grave is this close!

447
00:17:23,875 --> 00:17:25,500
Hurry up and spit it out already!

448
00:17:26,250 --> 00:17:26,875
The grave's...

449
00:17:27,041 --> 00:17:28,375
nearby.

450
00:17:28,375 --> 00:17:29,125
Shut up!

451
00:17:29,125 --> 00:17:30,208
Four fingers!

452
00:17:30,208 --> 00:17:32,375
I'll put you in the grave myself, wretch!

453
00:17:32,875 --> 00:17:35,333
What has this poor shoe-shine done to you?!

454
00:17:35,958 --> 00:17:38,000
Hurry take his food, he's hungry!

455
00:17:38,250 --> 00:17:39,291
Right away Sir, yes.

456
00:17:39,291 --> 00:17:40,083
Go on!

457
00:17:42,750 --> 00:17:44,333
Move it, idiot! Ow ow ow-

458
00:17:44,333 --> 00:17:46,333
♪ Chahargah Piece – Faramarz Payvar & Hossein Tehrani ♪

459
00:18:16,000 --> 00:18:17,000
Dear Uncle!

460
00:18:17,541 --> 00:18:18,833
Dear Uncle!

461
00:18:20,791 --> 00:18:21,666
Dear Uncle!

462
00:18:21,958 --> 00:18:22,625
Come!

463
00:18:23,833 --> 00:18:24,333
Dear Uncle!

464
00:18:24,583 --> 00:18:25,041
Run!

465
00:18:25,333 --> 00:18:26,125
Come!

466
00:18:26,541 --> 00:18:27,166
What is it?

467
00:18:27,208 --> 00:18:28,416
What's happened now? Dear Uncle!-

468
00:18:28,750 --> 00:18:29,791
This Indian Sardar came,

469
00:18:29,791 --> 00:18:31,375
he wants to throw the shoe-shine out.

470
00:18:31,375 --> 00:18:32,000
What?

471
00:18:32,666 --> 00:18:34,083
The Indian Sardar?

472
00:18:34,291 --> 00:18:36,708
Who does that Indian Sardar think he is!

473
00:18:37,000 --> 00:18:38,875
Run, tell Ghasem

474
00:18:38,916 --> 00:18:41,833
to ask this spy

475
00:18:41,875 --> 00:18:44,041
what business he has with this shoe-shine?

476
00:18:44,041 --> 00:18:46,833
Does Churchill own this alley or something?

477
00:18:46,875 --> 00:18:47,666
Mash Ghasem too,

478
00:18:47,666 --> 00:18:48,333
is in the alley.

479
00:18:48,666 --> 00:18:50,125
Then run, tell him

480
00:18:50,166 --> 00:18:52,791
to teach this spy a hard lesson!

481
00:18:52,916 --> 00:18:53,458
Saeed.

482
00:18:54,000 --> 00:18:56,000
Tell him not to mention my name!

483
00:18:56,000 --> 00:18:56,458
Yes!

484
00:18:56,458 --> 00:18:57,875
I know nothing.

485
00:19:00,583 --> 00:19:01,958
Strange!

486
00:19:02,583 --> 00:19:04,708
I should have thought of this Indian too.

487
00:19:05,333 --> 00:19:06,916
Either he knows,

488
00:19:07,458 --> 00:19:09,250
or it's London's order!

489
00:19:09,958 --> 00:19:14,125
God curse these English.

490
00:19:16,208 --> 00:19:17,416
This whole alley,

491
00:19:17,458 --> 00:19:18,666
is Sir's garden wall.

492
00:19:18,875 --> 00:19:20,000
This idol-worshipping infidel,

493
00:19:20,041 --> 00:19:21,875
as if he bought it, with that beard and fuzz of his.

494
00:19:21,958 --> 00:19:23,458
I am resident in this alley.

495
00:19:23,500 --> 00:19:25,541
I told you, our alley no need a shoe-shine.

496
00:19:26,666 --> 00:19:28,083
Well, obviously! My dear!-

497
00:19:28,083 --> 00:19:29,583
Don't you all walk barefoot?

498
00:19:29,583 --> 00:19:30,333
Yes, yes, yes!

499
00:19:30,375 --> 00:19:31,625
You don't even wear slippers!

500
00:19:31,666 --> 00:19:32,166
Yes, yes!

501
00:19:32,208 --> 00:19:32,458
Well!

502
00:19:32,500 --> 00:19:33,208
So what do you know

503
00:19:33,250 --> 00:19:34,583
what a shoe-shine is good for?

504
00:19:34,625 --> 00:19:35,166
Not at all! No, no!

505
00:19:35,208 --> 00:19:37,458
And you, stop yapping while Mr. Sardar is talking!

506
00:19:37,458 --> 00:19:38,250
Don't talk!

507
00:19:38,625 --> 00:19:39,375
Now mister Sardar!

508
00:19:39,416 --> 00:19:41,041
For the sake of your dear departed's souls,

509
00:19:41,083 --> 00:19:41,750
let this poor wretch too

510
00:19:41,750 --> 00:19:42,791
earn a crust of bread here!

511
00:19:42,833 --> 00:19:44,125
Their charity for the dead,

512
00:19:44,166 --> 00:19:45,833
let them give to their own city's beggars!

513
00:19:45,833 --> 00:19:46,791
We work,

514
00:19:46,833 --> 00:19:47,583
we sweat blood,

515
00:19:47,625 --> 00:19:48,750
we don't want charity either!

516
00:19:48,875 --> 00:19:50,875
Why you insult me did?

517
00:19:51,083 --> 00:19:52,583
This alley is not your place!

518
00:19:52,625 --> 00:19:53,625
You must went!

519
00:19:53,625 --> 00:19:55,166
I too took permission to sit here!

520
00:19:55,208 --> 00:19:56,708
Don't just stand, Saeed!

521
00:19:56,833 --> 00:19:57,875
Go help him!

522
00:19:58,000 --> 00:19:59,875
This Ghasem is so useless

523
00:19:59,916 --> 00:20:02,333
he can't even handle one Indian spy!

524
00:20:02,666 --> 00:20:03,708
Yes Dear Uncle!

525
00:20:04,333 --> 00:20:05,291
I'm not going from here,

526
00:20:05,333 --> 00:20:06,875
and it's none of your business either!

527
00:20:06,916 --> 00:20:07,958
Hey mister Sardar!

528
00:20:08,000 --> 00:20:08,416
Pack up, go!-

529
00:20:08,416 --> 00:20:10,416
This alley wants a shoe-shine and a cobbler.

530
00:20:10,583 --> 00:20:12,000
If it irks you so,

531
00:20:12,000 --> 00:20:13,541
I'll tell him to sit at our door!

532
00:20:13,833 --> 00:20:17,041
If I took up residence in this alley,

533
00:20:17,416 --> 00:20:18,791
it was for the quiet!

534
00:20:18,916 --> 00:20:19,916
But now you see?

535
00:20:19,958 --> 00:20:21,791
This little man here became a nuisance to my work!

536
00:20:22,250 --> 00:20:22,750
Hooligan!

537
00:20:22,791 --> 00:20:23,625
Go away, quick!

538
00:20:23,666 --> 00:20:24,500
The hooligan is you!

539
00:20:24,541 --> 00:20:26,708
(hubbub)

540
00:20:29,833 --> 00:20:30,916
Calm down!

541
00:20:30,958 --> 00:20:31,625
Hey, don't fight!

542
00:20:31,666 --> 00:20:33,541
Oh! What's going on?

543
00:20:33,583 --> 00:20:35,458
(hubbub)

544
00:20:35,500 --> 00:20:36,291
Enough already!

545
00:20:37,708 --> 00:20:38,333
Let go of each other!

546
00:20:38,375 --> 00:20:39,291
Leave him alone!

547
00:20:39,333 --> 00:20:41,333
(hubbub)

548
00:20:44,875 --> 00:20:45,791
Now I'll show you!

549
00:20:48,916 --> 00:20:50,375
I complaint against you make!

550
00:20:50,458 --> 00:20:51,000
Stop it!

551
00:20:51,041 --> 00:20:52,041
Let go of each other!

552
00:20:53,833 --> 00:20:55,333
They've got into a fight Uncle Asdollah!

553
00:20:57,208 --> 00:20:58,875
Hello Lady! What's the matter?

554
00:20:59,000 --> 00:21:00,583
Oh, I'm glad you came.

555
00:21:00,666 --> 00:21:02,833
Please stop them before it gets worst.

556
00:21:02,916 --> 00:21:03,833
Please!

557
00:21:04,291 --> 00:21:05,666
Stop them! Please!

558
00:21:05,666 --> 00:21:06,333
Moment!

559
00:21:07,416 --> 00:21:08,833
Moment! Moment!

560
00:21:08,875 --> 00:21:09,458
Enough, you stop!

561
00:21:09,500 --> 00:21:10,458
Step aside, let me see!

562
00:21:10,500 --> 00:21:10,916
Stop! Let go of me!-

563
00:21:10,958 --> 00:21:13,333
(hubbub)

564
00:21:13,583 --> 00:21:14,041
You let go of him!

565
00:21:14,083 --> 00:21:14,583
You let... you...

566
00:21:19,541 --> 00:21:20,291
Enough already!

567
00:21:21,833 --> 00:21:22,125
Moment!

568
00:21:22,125 --> 00:21:22,791
It's enough already!

569
00:21:25,750 --> 00:21:26,916
Take the Sardar upstairs!

570
00:21:27,583 --> 00:21:28,541
Let's go inside!

571
00:21:28,541 --> 00:21:29,750
Get out of the way!-

572
00:21:31,166 --> 00:21:32,083
Now you hit me?

573
00:21:32,833 --> 00:21:33,750
Enough already!

574
00:21:34,041 --> 00:21:35,708
What a disgraceful scene you've made!

575
00:21:38,166 --> 00:21:39,000
What is this?

576
00:21:54,833 --> 00:21:56,541
Never mind dear!

577
00:21:56,583 --> 00:21:58,666
Wherever you go, the first day there's always some fuss.

578
00:21:58,708 --> 00:22:00,958
Sir's notice of you is enough.

579
00:22:01,000 --> 00:22:03,291
Honestly, in this world I have God first,

580
00:22:03,291 --> 00:22:04,833
then Sir, then you.

581
00:22:05,625 --> 00:22:06,208
Rascal!

582
00:22:06,250 --> 00:22:07,208
In that fight

583
00:22:07,208 --> 00:22:08,916
you smacked my neck a couple times!

584
00:22:08,958 --> 00:22:09,666
What got into you?

585
00:22:09,708 --> 00:22:10,666
Why lie!

586
00:22:10,666 --> 00:22:12,458
The grave is this close!

587
00:22:12,791 --> 00:22:14,500
If not for Mr. Asdollah-Mirza,

588
00:22:14,541 --> 00:22:15,958
I'd have pulped him!

589
00:22:15,958 --> 00:22:18,000
I just don't like to raise my fists!

590
00:22:18,166 --> 00:22:20,416
I'm a match for a hundred of these Indians!

591
00:22:20,458 --> 00:22:20,875
One day...

592
00:22:20,875 --> 00:22:22,125
Moment! Mash Ghasem...

593
00:22:22,166 --> 00:22:23,291
Run a glass...

594
00:22:23,333 --> 00:22:24,750
Run, get a glass of cold sherbet,

595
00:22:24,791 --> 00:22:25,791
for Houshang Khan,

596
00:22:25,833 --> 00:22:26,416
to wet his throat.

597
00:22:26,416 --> 00:22:27,541
Lemon or sour-cherry sherbet? Run, go...-

598
00:22:27,583 --> 00:22:28,250
Lemon!

599
00:22:28,291 --> 00:22:28,958
Yes!

600
00:22:29,583 --> 00:22:30,916
Sit at your work with a quiet heart.

601
00:22:30,916 --> 00:22:32,125
You too don't be upset anymore.

602
00:22:32,125 --> 00:22:32,541
Here you are.

603
00:22:32,583 --> 00:22:35,125
Sir, I'm no willow to tremble in every wind!

604
00:22:35,125 --> 00:22:36,458
(Sound of the people’s hubbub)

605
00:22:36,500 --> 00:22:38,916
Shir-Ali, I hear he's stirred up the quarter!

606
00:22:40,333 --> 00:22:41,875
What's going on, Sir?

607
00:22:41,875 --> 00:22:44,541
What's this shoe-shine's problem, shooting his mouth off? It's nothing!-

608
00:22:44,791 --> 00:22:48,041
Am I dead, that he stirs up the quarter?!

609
00:22:48,291 --> 00:22:49,791
I'll hit him over the head with this carcass so hard

610
00:22:49,833 --> 00:22:51,541
both his eyes will pop out at his feet!

611
00:22:51,791 --> 00:22:53,833
A lowlife stirs up our quarter?

612
00:22:54,166 --> 00:22:55,375
Bless those strong hands of yours!

613
00:22:55,458 --> 00:22:57,875
I haven't had a chance to ask after you lately.

614
00:22:57,916 --> 00:22:59,000
How are you, Shir-Ali?

615
00:22:59,041 --> 00:22:59,750
All well, I hope?

616
00:22:59,791 --> 00:23:00,708
How's the missus?

617
00:23:00,708 --> 00:23:01,791
She's at your service!

618
00:23:01,833 --> 00:23:03,041
I'm your servant too.

619
00:23:03,083 --> 00:23:04,583
Don't say that, Mr. Shir-Ali!

620
00:23:04,583 --> 00:23:06,750
So Sir, what's this shoe-shine kid's story?

621
00:23:06,750 --> 00:23:07,791
Do we know?

622
00:23:07,833 --> 00:23:08,583
He's a good kid!

623
00:23:08,625 --> 00:23:09,708
I know him.

624
00:23:09,750 --> 00:23:12,291
The poor thing came here to earn a crust of bread.

625
00:23:12,500 --> 00:23:13,083
In any case,

626
00:23:13,125 --> 00:23:14,041
we all have polishing

627
00:23:14,083 --> 00:23:16,041
and shoe repair, that sort of thing.

628
00:23:16,083 --> 00:23:17,458
Let it go, Shir-Ali...

629
00:23:17,625 --> 00:23:19,625
I don't think, out of fear of you, he'll dare

630
00:23:19,625 --> 00:23:20,875
raise his voice.

631
00:23:20,875 --> 00:23:21,791
Please, come in.

632
00:23:21,791 --> 00:23:22,500
Gentlemen, come.

633
00:23:22,541 --> 00:23:23,000
Take care.

634
00:23:23,000 --> 00:23:23,750
Welcome.

635
00:23:27,666 --> 00:23:28,708
All ended well.

636
00:23:28,916 --> 00:23:31,000
Sir, I fear no bully.

637
00:23:31,333 --> 00:23:33,250
From above, I was told to stay here,

638
00:23:33,291 --> 00:23:34,416
and here I stay.

639
00:23:35,541 --> 00:23:36,583
Whoever has the nerve,

640
00:23:36,583 --> 00:23:38,041
let him come and move me!

641
00:23:40,583 --> 00:23:41,875
Who above told you?

642
00:23:41,875 --> 00:23:42,916
The One above

643
00:23:42,958 --> 00:23:44,791
who decides where a man earns his living!

644
00:23:45,500 --> 00:23:46,041
Yes!

645
00:23:46,250 --> 00:23:46,708
Yes!

646
00:23:47,166 --> 00:23:48,666
Where do you sleep at night?

647
00:23:49,041 --> 00:23:49,875
Coffeehouse.

648
00:23:50,291 --> 00:23:51,208
Across the street.

649
00:23:51,666 --> 00:23:52,625
It's where the poor folk stay.

650
00:23:52,708 --> 00:23:53,125
Good.

651
00:23:53,416 --> 00:23:53,958
Good.

652
00:23:55,166 --> 00:23:56,666
Always stay around here.

653
00:23:57,541 --> 00:23:58,500
Now eat your lunch.

654
00:23:58,833 --> 00:23:59,833
Eat before it gets cold.

655
00:24:01,708 --> 00:24:02,166
Here you are.

656
00:24:02,208 --> 00:24:02,625
Bon appétit.

657
00:24:02,666 --> 00:24:03,166
A morsel.

658
00:24:03,166 --> 00:24:04,458
No no no. I'm not hungry.

659
00:24:04,458 --> 00:24:05,333
Thanks.

660
00:24:09,708 --> 00:24:11,583
Your Dear Uncle's mind is a bit more at ease.

661
00:24:11,625 --> 00:24:12,250
Your Agha Jan too,

662
00:24:12,291 --> 00:24:12,791
I don't think,

663
00:24:12,791 --> 00:24:14,875
can pull a new trick for now.

664
00:24:14,916 --> 00:24:16,083
And as for Leili.

665
00:24:16,541 --> 00:24:18,166
You must, as soon as possible...

666
00:24:19,041 --> 00:24:19,750
What's up?

667
00:24:20,416 --> 00:24:21,125
Please.

668
00:24:21,166 --> 00:24:21,875
What happened Dear Uncle?

669
00:24:22,291 --> 00:24:23,041
What's the matter?

670
00:24:23,125 --> 00:24:23,875
Please!

671
00:24:23,916 --> 00:24:24,875
Why is the lady crying?

672
00:24:25,208 --> 00:24:26,708
Shaz, say something to her.

673
00:24:26,708 --> 00:24:28,583
She's been crying for an hour now!

674
00:24:29,125 --> 00:24:30,708
Why? What happened?

675
00:24:30,958 --> 00:24:32,208
If you remember,

676
00:24:32,250 --> 00:24:34,166
when Puri went to Ahvaz for service,

677
00:24:34,208 --> 00:24:35,791
we had no news of him for a while.

678
00:24:36,125 --> 00:24:37,375
So I wrote a letter

679
00:24:37,416 --> 00:24:39,208
to one of my friends who's in Ahvaz,

680
00:24:39,208 --> 00:24:40,041
asking him to find out

681
00:24:40,083 --> 00:24:41,833
how Puri was and write to us.

682
00:24:41,833 --> 00:24:42,958
Now his answer came.

683
00:24:42,958 --> 00:24:44,208
What did he write Dear Uncle?

684
00:24:44,583 --> 00:24:46,083
He wrote Puri is sick!

685
00:24:46,125 --> 00:24:47,375
No, he isn't sick.

686
00:24:47,500 --> 00:24:48,333
Whatever I say,

687
00:24:48,333 --> 00:24:50,333
Puri himself wrote a letter recently,

688
00:24:50,583 --> 00:24:51,750
she still doesn't get it!

689
00:24:51,958 --> 00:24:53,458
Isn't Puri's letter dated?

690
00:24:53,458 --> 00:24:53,875
No!

691
00:24:54,041 --> 00:24:56,125
That's why she doesn't believe it!

692
00:24:56,125 --> 00:24:58,250
She says this is from his old letters!

693
00:24:58,666 --> 00:24:59,375
What kind of talk?

694
00:24:59,708 --> 00:25:00,291
Shazdeh!

695
00:25:00,791 --> 00:25:01,458
Shazdeh!

696
00:25:01,500 --> 00:25:03,000
I'd give my life for you.

697
00:25:03,041 --> 00:25:04,125
Do something.

698
00:25:04,125 --> 00:25:05,583
Send a telegram!

699
00:25:09,625 --> 00:25:11,291
So what is Puri-jun's illness?

700
00:25:11,291 --> 00:25:12,250
He's fine!

701
00:25:12,625 --> 00:25:14,208
But the lady won't believe it!

702
00:25:14,250 --> 00:25:15,583
How is he fine?

703
00:25:16,875 --> 00:25:18,125
Puri-jun...

704
00:25:18,291 --> 00:25:19,458
Puri-jun...

705
00:25:20,375 --> 00:25:22,708
Your mother would give her life for you.

706
00:25:23,708 --> 00:25:25,708
Why don't you believe my word?

707
00:25:26,083 --> 00:25:29,000
So my friend in Ahvaz wrote some nonsense!

708
00:25:29,041 --> 00:25:30,166
You believed it, lady?

709
00:25:31,000 --> 00:25:32,708
My child heard gunfire,

710
00:25:32,750 --> 00:25:33,708
and panicked!

711
00:25:33,958 --> 00:25:34,750
God kill me

712
00:25:34,791 --> 00:25:37,750
for letting my child go to this war and chaos!

713
00:25:37,750 --> 00:25:39,333
Why talk nonsense, woman!

714
00:25:40,833 --> 00:25:42,416
I said that my friend from Ahvaz,

715
00:25:42,416 --> 00:25:43,750
wrote nonsense

716
00:25:44,041 --> 00:25:45,208
Puri-jun is not a child,

717
00:25:45,250 --> 00:25:46,958
to fear cannons and rifles.

718
00:25:47,208 --> 00:25:49,916
He must've eaten bad food and got sick.

719
00:25:50,041 --> 00:25:50,416
And now,

720
00:25:50,416 --> 00:25:52,875
or one night he went drinking arak with his friends!

721
00:25:52,916 --> 00:25:54,875
He overdid it and got sick!

722
00:25:54,916 --> 00:25:56,458
But Puri-jun doesn't drink!

723
00:25:56,500 --> 00:25:58,375
Anyway, Puri is my son!

724
00:25:58,416 --> 00:25:59,458
I know him!

725
00:25:59,875 --> 00:26:01,375
Among a thousand young men

726
00:26:01,416 --> 00:26:03,541
you won't find Puri's heart and nerve!

727
00:26:03,583 --> 00:26:05,625
Madam! The Colonel is right!

728
00:26:06,041 --> 00:26:07,166
In the middle of a million youths,

729
00:26:07,166 --> 00:26:08,416
there isn't one like Puri!

730
00:26:08,500 --> 00:26:09,625
In Puri's destiny,

731
00:26:09,625 --> 00:26:11,375
I see a Julius Caesar!

732
00:26:11,375 --> 00:26:11,916
Shazdeh!

733
00:26:12,125 --> 00:26:13,583
You, for all your faults,

734
00:26:13,708 --> 00:26:14,708
have one merit!

735
00:26:15,041 --> 00:26:16,375
Judging men!

736
00:26:16,666 --> 00:26:17,291
Bravo!

737
00:26:17,458 --> 00:26:18,166
Bravo!

738
00:26:20,791 --> 00:26:22,041
Well, for now goodbye!

739
00:26:22,875 --> 00:26:23,791
Let's go, dear.

740
00:26:24,125 --> 00:26:25,625
If no news comes by tomorrow,

741
00:26:26,041 --> 00:26:27,750
I'll have to go to Ahvaz myself.

742
00:26:28,041 --> 00:26:28,583
Yes lady!

743
00:26:29,375 --> 00:26:29,958
It's a good thought!

744
00:26:29,958 --> 00:26:31,458
There's no need for all this crying.

745
00:26:32,875 --> 00:26:33,625
Hold!

746
00:26:34,000 --> 00:26:34,708
Hold!

747
00:26:36,000 --> 00:26:38,166
Julius Caesar returns from Ahvaz any day now,

748
00:26:38,208 --> 00:26:40,291
Better do something fast, Mark Antony!

749
00:26:40,333 --> 00:26:42,333
Don't just sit there like a klutz watching!

750
00:26:42,708 --> 00:26:44,208
They'll take Cleopatra, you know!

751
00:26:44,250 --> 00:26:45,541
But what should I do, Uncle Asdollah?

752
00:26:45,541 --> 00:26:46,708
How often must I say it?

753
00:26:47,125 --> 00:26:47,875
Hey, what'd you say?

754
00:26:47,916 --> 00:26:49,125
Open your ears Mark Antony!

755
00:26:49,125 --> 00:26:49,750
Take her on a trip,

756
00:26:49,750 --> 00:26:51,583
San... Fran... cis... co!

757
00:26:51,625 --> 00:26:52,750
Ah! Uncle Asdollah!

758
00:26:59,750 --> 00:27:01,541
Let's go to the registry office and settle this!-

759
00:27:01,625 --> 00:27:02,333
Your place,

760
00:27:02,333 --> 00:27:03,375
is your brother's house,

761
00:27:03,583 --> 00:27:04,583
or my house!

762
00:27:08,750 --> 00:27:09,875
Be considerate!

763
00:27:09,916 --> 00:27:11,041
It's shameful to tell people

764
00:27:11,041 --> 00:27:12,708
Puri-jun panicked at the sound of a gunshot!

765
00:27:12,708 --> 00:27:13,666
Hello Khan Dadash!

766
00:27:14,291 --> 00:27:16,083
Sir! Sir, I'm begging you!

767
00:27:16,125 --> 00:27:17,083
I'm afraid it'll be late!

768
00:27:17,083 --> 00:27:18,000
Puri is sick!

769
00:27:18,083 --> 00:27:20,666
I fear harm will come to my darling boy!

770
00:27:21,083 --> 00:27:22,166
Let go of me now!

771
00:27:22,458 --> 00:27:23,833
Talk tonight, Khan Dadash!-

772
00:27:23,833 --> 00:27:24,458
Now I have work! Khan Dadash!-

773
00:27:24,500 --> 00:27:26,375
What do you think if I go to Ahvaz myself?

774
00:27:26,416 --> 00:27:26,708
Yes?

775
00:27:27,875 --> 00:27:30,833
Is this any time for a trip,

776
00:27:30,875 --> 00:27:32,375
dear Colonel!

777
00:27:32,750 --> 00:27:35,000
The trench must not be left empty! But Puri-jun is sick!-

778
00:27:35,041 --> 00:27:36,541
I'm worried for him!

779
00:27:37,000 --> 00:27:39,000
This is a trick!

780
00:27:39,166 --> 00:27:41,708
This too is a trick of the English,

781
00:27:41,708 --> 00:27:45,500
to get you all away from me,

782
00:27:45,666 --> 00:27:48,250
so I'm alone and they can

783
00:27:48,291 --> 00:27:51,041
carry out their sinister plans!

784
00:27:51,041 --> 00:27:55,500
They say their army is already near Tehran!

785
00:27:59,250 --> 00:28:01,250
(Sound of knocking at the door)

786
00:28:13,625 --> 00:28:14,291
Didn't you hear?

787
00:28:14,333 --> 00:28:14,875
What is it? What happened?

788
00:28:14,916 --> 00:28:15,208
Did you hear?

789
00:28:15,250 --> 00:28:15,500
What?

790
00:28:15,541 --> 00:28:16,166
The radio!

791
00:28:16,250 --> 00:28:16,833
What's happened?

792
00:28:17,041 --> 00:28:17,708
They arrived!

793
00:28:17,750 --> 00:28:19,000
They arrived!

794
00:28:19,125 --> 00:28:21,958
They read the government's statement on the radio!

795
00:28:22,166 --> 00:28:26,166
The English reached Tehran!

796
00:28:26,166 --> 00:28:27,750
(The doctor laughs)

797
00:28:28,083 --> 00:28:30,458
There's no reason to be so worried!

798
00:28:31,375 --> 00:28:34,041
You yourselves, know the English better than I

799
00:28:34,208 --> 00:28:37,708
They never, openly attack from the front!

800
00:28:38,125 --> 00:28:41,250
I know this deceitful wolf well!

801
00:28:41,625 --> 00:28:45,666
I know they always stab you in the back!

802
00:28:45,958 --> 00:28:47,666
This I know well!

803
00:28:48,000 --> 00:28:51,500
I've spent my life fighting England!

804
00:28:51,541 --> 00:28:52,541
Now if you know the English,

805
00:28:52,583 --> 00:28:53,666
why are you so upset?

806
00:28:54,125 --> 00:28:55,583
Oh, sir!

807
00:28:55,625 --> 00:28:58,875
I'm not upset for my own sake!

808
00:28:59,458 --> 00:29:01,541
My duty is clear!

809
00:29:01,791 --> 00:29:04,375
Whether I'm here or there,

810
00:29:04,458 --> 00:29:07,333
I can't escape them!

811
00:29:08,333 --> 00:29:11,291
I'm not grieving for myself!

812
00:29:11,375 --> 00:29:15,000
A thousand like me, sacrificed for Iran!

813
00:29:15,333 --> 00:29:18,625
I grieve for my country!

814
00:29:18,833 --> 00:29:20,041
Woe!

815
00:29:20,125 --> 00:29:23,875
Alas, if Iran should become

816
00:29:24,083 --> 00:29:27,083
a ruined den of leopards and lions!

817
00:29:27,458 --> 00:29:28,166
Surely,

818
00:29:28,166 --> 00:29:29,833
any day now

819
00:29:29,833 --> 00:29:32,750
they'll exile all the freedom-lovers from the country!

820
00:29:32,791 --> 00:29:34,083
Well, what can one do?

821
00:29:34,166 --> 00:29:35,375
As you say:

822
00:29:35,416 --> 00:29:38,583
In the claws of a bloodthirsty lion,

823
00:29:39,083 --> 00:29:41,708
what choice is there but to surrender?

824
00:29:42,208 --> 00:29:42,916
No!

825
00:29:43,291 --> 00:29:43,916
It's no use.

826
00:29:44,416 --> 00:29:46,041
Nothing can be done.

827
00:29:47,208 --> 00:29:48,250
But...

828
00:29:48,666 --> 00:29:51,125
But I want to ask you a favor.

829
00:29:51,500 --> 00:29:52,875
Could you order

830
00:29:52,875 --> 00:29:54,666
the door be shut tight?

831
00:29:55,583 --> 00:29:58,416
Between my house and yours there is no wall.

832
00:29:58,750 --> 00:30:01,625
We all use one door to come and go.

833
00:30:01,750 --> 00:30:06,083
I'll make sure to tell Ghasem

834
00:30:06,125 --> 00:30:08,166
that the garden door,

835
00:30:08,458 --> 00:30:11,625
is not to be opened to strangers!

836
00:30:11,750 --> 00:30:15,791
Especially the children must not leave the house!

837
00:30:16,625 --> 00:30:18,916
They have no business with your children.

838
00:30:19,083 --> 00:30:21,583
Their target is me!

839
00:30:21,750 --> 00:30:23,791
My innocent Leili...

840
00:30:28,750 --> 00:30:30,958
(He chuckles)

841
00:30:35,916 --> 00:30:39,375
♪ Rhythmic music ♪

842
00:30:40,041 --> 00:30:40,916
Saeed!

843
00:30:41,375 --> 00:30:42,125
Saeed!

844
00:30:42,375 --> 00:30:42,958
Yes Dear Uncle?

845
00:30:43,000 --> 00:30:43,625
Saeed!

846
00:30:44,291 --> 00:30:45,125
Come, son. Yes!-

847
00:30:45,458 --> 00:30:46,250
Saeed-jun!

848
00:30:46,541 --> 00:30:48,250
You're a big boy, son.

849
00:30:48,250 --> 00:30:50,916
Things are happening around us!

850
00:30:51,166 --> 00:30:52,583
Maybe you...

851
00:30:52,791 --> 00:30:57,125
maybe you can't grasp how dire things are!

852
00:30:57,333 --> 00:30:59,041
I beg you,

853
00:30:59,250 --> 00:31:02,041
if any stranger asks about me,

854
00:31:02,083 --> 00:31:03,916
don't answer at all!

855
00:31:04,666 --> 00:31:05,833
The garden door,

856
00:31:05,875 --> 00:31:08,208
don't open it to any stranger!

857
00:31:08,375 --> 00:31:09,541
What happened Dear Uncle?

858
00:31:09,583 --> 00:31:11,041
What do you think happened?

859
00:31:11,125 --> 00:31:13,000
The enemy arrived!

860
00:31:16,833 --> 00:31:17,958
My son...

861
00:31:18,333 --> 00:31:19,583
Every time you

862
00:31:19,791 --> 00:31:20,916
see your uncle,

863
00:31:21,500 --> 00:31:22,500
it may be,

864
00:31:22,666 --> 00:31:24,416
the last time.

865
00:31:24,791 --> 00:31:25,833
Of course,

866
00:31:26,083 --> 00:31:27,708
remember my son,

867
00:31:28,208 --> 00:31:30,875
these are the rules of the struggle.

868
00:31:31,208 --> 00:31:33,208
♪ Rhythmic music ♪

869
00:32:03,875 --> 00:32:04,500
Where is he?

870
00:32:05,333 --> 00:32:06,083
Where is he?

871
00:32:06,458 --> 00:32:07,500
Where did he go?

872
00:32:07,875 --> 00:32:08,750
Ghasem!

873
00:32:08,916 --> 00:32:10,250
Where did he go?

874
00:32:10,500 --> 00:32:11,333
Ghasem!

875
00:32:11,375 --> 00:32:12,166
Yes Sir?

876
00:32:12,333 --> 00:32:12,833
Where is he?

877
00:32:12,958 --> 00:32:13,625
Huh?

878
00:32:14,041 --> 00:32:14,833
Where did he go?

879
00:32:14,916 --> 00:32:15,666
Who is where?

880
00:32:16,000 --> 00:32:16,833
This shoe-shine!

881
00:32:16,875 --> 00:32:17,666
Houshang Khan!

882
00:32:17,833 --> 00:32:18,625
He's right here Sir.

883
00:32:18,708 --> 00:32:19,583
He isn't!

884
00:32:19,916 --> 00:32:20,541
Where is he?

885
00:32:20,708 --> 00:32:21,708
Where did he go?

886
00:32:21,958 --> 00:32:22,750
He's right here.

887
00:32:22,875 --> 00:32:24,125
I say he isn't!

888
00:32:24,791 --> 00:32:27,208
After lunch, I went and got his dishes, Sir!

889
00:32:27,375 --> 00:32:28,916
Then where is he? Where did he go?

890
00:32:29,166 --> 00:32:30,625
If you ask me,

891
00:32:30,666 --> 00:32:32,166
he was a jackass shoe-shine.

892
00:32:32,500 --> 00:32:34,000
If you want shoes shined, Sir,

893
00:32:34,000 --> 00:32:35,416
give them, I'll take them to the little bazaar,

894
00:32:35,458 --> 00:32:36,750
and be right back.

895
00:32:37,000 --> 00:32:39,083
Honestly Sir, he shines badly!

896
00:32:39,250 --> 00:32:41,208
Seems better to let him go.

897
00:32:41,291 --> 00:32:42,125
Fool!

898
00:32:42,166 --> 00:32:44,333
I ask you where is he?

899
00:32:44,458 --> 00:32:45,625
Where did he go?

900
00:32:45,666 --> 00:32:47,291
I want to know how, unannounced,

901
00:32:47,333 --> 00:32:49,333
where the hell he's gone!

902
00:32:49,416 --> 00:32:50,541
Sir, why lie!

903
00:32:50,583 --> 00:32:52,458
The grave is this close!

904
00:32:53,000 --> 00:32:54,791
I didn't see him with my own eyes.

905
00:32:54,875 --> 00:32:57,041
Want me to go see where the hell he's gone?

906
00:32:57,291 --> 00:32:58,541
Then hurry!

907
00:32:58,541 --> 00:33:01,833
Run, quick, bring me news!

908
00:33:02,083 --> 00:33:03,583
Shut the door behind you!

909
00:33:06,291 --> 00:33:07,041
Saeed!

910
00:33:07,208 --> 00:33:08,625
Run, son, come here!

911
00:33:08,666 --> 00:33:09,458
Run, run!

912
00:33:10,541 --> 00:33:11,541
What is it Dear Uncle? Eh... Baba-jun!-

913
00:33:11,750 --> 00:33:13,125
That idiot Ghasem!

914
00:33:13,250 --> 00:33:14,916
Run to the little bazaar yourself,

915
00:33:15,000 --> 00:33:16,416
and ask people, ask the grocer,

916
00:33:16,500 --> 00:33:19,083
where this shoe-shine went!

917
00:33:19,333 --> 00:33:20,916
Why are you getting so worked up?

918
00:33:21,041 --> 00:33:22,875
I...I...I... I'm fine, son!

919
00:33:23,500 --> 00:33:27,541
He had a new pair of my European shoes,

920
00:33:27,666 --> 00:33:29,125
I'd given them for polish.

921
00:33:29,125 --> 00:33:30,125
Now you run!

922
00:33:30,541 --> 00:33:31,500
and find him, son. Yes!-

923
00:33:31,541 --> 00:33:32,125
Run my dear!

924
00:33:32,458 --> 00:33:34,625
Eh! Mash Ghasem! Ghasem did you find him? What happened?-

925
00:33:34,750 --> 00:33:35,250
Where?

926
00:33:35,791 --> 00:33:36,916
Sir, why lie!

927
00:33:36,958 --> 00:33:38,583
The grave is this close!

928
00:33:38,708 --> 00:33:40,416
To hell with lies!

929
00:33:40,541 --> 00:33:41,833
Speak!

930
00:33:42,375 --> 00:33:44,541
Honestly Sir! Abram Sir was just...

931
00:33:44,750 --> 00:33:46,416
you know, the haberdasher!

932
00:33:46,625 --> 00:33:48,291
Speak!

933
00:33:48,458 --> 00:33:49,958
Brainless idiot!

934
00:33:50,000 --> 00:33:52,500
Did you find him or not?

935
00:33:52,708 --> 00:33:55,125
Honestly Sir! From what Abram Sir was saying,

936
00:33:55,333 --> 00:33:58,541
Abbas the policeman took him to the police station.

937
00:33:59,375 --> 00:34:00,375
The police?!

938
00:34:01,041 --> 00:34:01,750
Why?

939
00:34:01,875 --> 00:34:02,875
What did he do?

940
00:34:03,375 --> 00:34:04,291
Sir, why lie!

941
00:34:04,375 --> 00:34:06,125
The grave is this close!

942
00:34:06,791 --> 00:34:09,041
I didn't see anything with my own eyes!

943
00:34:09,625 --> 00:34:11,791
But from what Mr. Abram Sir was saying,

944
00:34:12,000 --> 00:34:13,291
he stole a watch!

945
00:34:13,416 --> 00:34:14,208
A watch?

946
00:34:14,625 --> 00:34:15,750
You could tell from his eyes

947
00:34:15,791 --> 00:34:18,916
he was a thief and a lecher, Sir!

948
00:34:19,333 --> 00:34:20,541
A watch!

949
00:34:20,875 --> 00:34:22,916
Whose watch did he steal?

950
00:34:23,250 --> 00:34:24,166
The fellow...

951
00:34:24,416 --> 00:34:27,666
the Indian Sardar complained to the police!

952
00:34:28,000 --> 00:34:29,625
He said that in today's brawl

953
00:34:29,625 --> 00:34:31,500
someone stole the watch from his pocket!

954
00:34:32,083 --> 00:34:35,000
His watch was gold, Sir!

955
00:34:35,958 --> 00:34:37,791
Shameless!

956
00:34:38,083 --> 00:34:41,166
I knew they were waiting for a day like this!

957
00:34:41,166 --> 00:34:41,916
Who Sir?

958
00:34:42,000 --> 00:34:44,083
The English!

959
00:34:45,625 --> 00:34:47,000
By Imam Ali, I pray

960
00:34:47,041 --> 00:34:48,791
they never know a moment's peace!

961
00:34:50,333 --> 00:34:51,750
They started!

962
00:34:53,375 --> 00:34:55,791
They stab you in the back!

963
00:35:02,791 --> 00:35:03,958
O God!

964
00:35:04,791 --> 00:35:06,916
I put myself in your hands.

965
00:35:07,375 --> 00:35:09,375
♪ Sad traditional music ♪

966
00:35:39,541 --> 00:35:41,333
(Hubbub of the gathering)

967
00:35:46,083 --> 00:35:47,666
What are you doing Khan Dadash?

968
00:35:47,750 --> 00:35:49,750
Things are not normal these days!

969
00:35:49,875 --> 00:35:52,291
One must be very careful!

970
00:35:52,958 --> 00:35:54,291
Everyone is waiting for you!

971
00:35:54,333 --> 00:35:55,333
You go join them,

972
00:35:55,333 --> 00:35:56,291
I'll be right there.

973
00:35:56,291 --> 00:35:57,541
Very well, so be it.

974
00:35:57,875 --> 00:35:59,875
(Sound of the guests’ laughter)

975
00:36:09,000 --> 00:36:11,500
Well, well! Khan Dadash has arrived!

976
00:36:11,750 --> 00:36:12,250
Come in!

977
00:36:12,541 --> 00:36:13,083
Hello Dear Uncle.

978
00:36:13,083 --> 00:36:13,791
Hello my dear!

979
00:36:13,833 --> 00:36:15,125
I apologize to you all

980
00:36:15,166 --> 00:36:16,333
for being late. Hello, sir-

981
00:36:16,458 --> 00:36:17,250
Hello.

982
00:36:17,250 --> 00:36:17,833
Please.

983
00:36:17,875 --> 00:36:19,125
How are you, Doctor?

984
00:36:19,291 --> 00:36:21,083
You look in great spirits. Thank God, I'm not bad.

985
00:36:21,083 --> 00:36:23,500
The face reveals what's in the heart!

986
00:36:23,500 --> 00:36:25,458
Seems you were deep in talk!

987
00:36:25,500 --> 00:36:27,666
Sir! Happy news ahead!

988
00:36:27,750 --> 00:36:28,916
We were saying Puri-jun,

989
00:36:28,958 --> 00:36:31,458
God bless him a thousand times, is a grown man now!

990
00:36:31,500 --> 00:36:34,333
And now that he's coming back safe from Ahvaz,

991
00:36:34,416 --> 00:36:36,791
the Colonel must roll up his sleeves

992
00:36:36,833 --> 00:36:39,625
as soon as possible, get the wedding

993
00:36:39,666 --> 00:36:40,958
under way.

994
00:36:42,958 --> 00:36:44,250
You don't know, these days,

995
00:36:44,250 --> 00:36:45,875
in this war and turmoil,

996
00:36:45,916 --> 00:36:47,458
what we suffered!

997
00:36:48,958 --> 00:36:51,125
Poor thing, Puri was sick.

998
00:36:51,416 --> 00:36:52,125
In Ahvaz!

999
00:36:52,291 --> 00:36:53,291
Far from home!

1000
00:36:53,625 --> 00:36:54,666
No mail...

1001
00:36:54,750 --> 00:36:56,416
the telegraph office was closed!

1002
00:36:57,166 --> 00:36:59,791
You don't know what we endured!

1003
00:37:00,333 --> 00:37:02,833
Till at last, his letter came today.

1004
00:37:03,041 --> 00:37:04,416
Well, thank God!

1005
00:37:04,458 --> 00:37:05,500
Thank God!

1006
00:37:05,541 --> 00:37:06,416
Now if,

1007
00:37:06,500 --> 00:37:08,041
Sir permits,

1008
00:37:08,041 --> 00:37:09,625
by the will of God,

1009
00:37:09,708 --> 00:37:13,125
at Eid al-Adha, we'll hold the engagement.

1010
00:37:22,750 --> 00:37:24,041
Whatever he says.-

1011
00:37:24,083 --> 00:37:24,916
Yes, of course!

1012
00:37:27,041 --> 00:37:27,875
Cheers,

1013
00:37:27,916 --> 00:37:29,750
Have you picked out a bride for him too?

1014
00:37:30,375 --> 00:37:32,000
You don't know, Asdollah?!

1015
00:37:32,375 --> 00:37:33,208
Moment!

1016
00:37:33,250 --> 00:37:34,958
How would I know?!

1017
00:37:35,583 --> 00:37:36,208
Besides!

1018
00:37:36,208 --> 00:37:38,791
I doubt a conscript soldier

1019
00:37:38,833 --> 00:37:40,625
just back from service,

1020
00:37:40,666 --> 00:37:43,166
with no proper job yet,

1021
00:37:43,208 --> 00:37:44,458
can find a wife!

1022
00:37:44,791 --> 00:37:46,916
Puri-jun must first support himself!

1023
00:37:47,083 --> 00:37:49,500
What kind of talk is that? Nonsense!

1024
00:37:49,541 --> 00:37:52,166
With Puri-jun's higher education,

1025
00:37:52,208 --> 00:37:53,833
all the government offices,

1026
00:37:53,875 --> 00:37:55,750
will snap him up.

1027
00:37:56,083 --> 00:37:57,541
It's no joke.

1028
00:37:58,083 --> 00:38:00,875
The boy studied 15-16 years

1029
00:38:00,916 --> 00:38:02,208
got his degree!

1030
00:38:02,833 --> 00:38:03,458
On your life,

1031
00:38:03,458 --> 00:38:04,708
all my friends,

1032
00:38:04,750 --> 00:38:06,416
who work in the government offices,

1033
00:38:06,416 --> 00:38:09,958
are begging to take Puri on!

1034
00:38:10,041 --> 00:38:12,625
Don't think I'm praising my own son!

1035
00:38:12,666 --> 00:38:14,458
This boy is truly a genius!

1036
00:38:14,958 --> 00:38:16,583
That's obvious from his face!

1037
00:38:16,583 --> 00:38:18,583
Whose daughter have you picked out for him?

1038
00:38:18,583 --> 00:38:20,583
Girls should dream

1039
00:38:20,583 --> 00:38:22,250
to be Puri-jun's wife!

1040
00:38:22,583 --> 00:38:24,083
Although Qamar

1041
00:38:24,250 --> 00:38:27,666
is my stepdaughter and I can't give her hand,

1042
00:38:27,916 --> 00:38:29,125
believe me,

1043
00:38:29,166 --> 00:38:30,791
if Puri says the word,

1044
00:38:30,833 --> 00:38:32,833
I'll get Aziz's permission! Splendid!-

1045
00:38:33,250 --> 00:38:34,041
Congratulations!

1046
00:38:34,083 --> 00:38:35,625
So there'll be an engagement?

1047
00:38:37,208 --> 00:38:38,291
Mister Dust-Ali!

1048
00:38:39,041 --> 00:38:41,375
Puri-jun has someone else in mind.

1049
00:38:44,041 --> 00:38:47,166
Cousins' marriages are made in heaven.

1050
00:38:47,208 --> 00:38:48,833
As they've said since olden times!

1051
00:38:48,875 --> 00:38:50,333
Moment! Moment!

1052
00:38:50,500 --> 00:38:52,166
Your servant objects!

1053
00:38:52,500 --> 00:38:54,625
Leili-jun is only 14 or 15!

1054
00:38:54,666 --> 00:38:56,416
She's far from done with school!

1055
00:38:56,458 --> 00:38:57,458
I want to know,

1056
00:38:57,458 --> 00:38:59,666
His Highness Shazdeh Asdollah-Mirza,

1057
00:38:59,708 --> 00:39:01,125
when he took a wife,

1058
00:39:01,250 --> 00:39:02,708
had he finished studying?

1059
00:39:02,750 --> 00:39:03,375
Shut up!

1060
00:39:03,416 --> 00:39:04,833
Brother, please!

1061
00:39:04,833 --> 00:39:05,541
Dust-Ali!

1062
00:39:05,583 --> 00:39:06,583
Don't you ever again

1063
00:39:06,583 --> 00:39:08,791
mention Asdollah's wife!

1064
00:39:10,541 --> 00:39:11,125
Dust-Ali!

1065
00:39:11,166 --> 00:39:11,750
Please!

1066
00:39:11,791 --> 00:39:13,125
Don't make such a fuss!

1067
00:39:21,000 --> 00:39:23,458
Uncle Asdollah! You have a wife, huh?

1068
00:39:29,833 --> 00:39:31,583
How nosy you are kid!

1069
00:39:35,166 --> 00:39:37,916
With all this talk of wives, marriage and weddings,

1070
00:39:37,916 --> 00:39:38,708
a man forgets,

1071
00:39:38,750 --> 00:39:40,958
that he's living in wartime.

1072
00:39:42,833 --> 00:39:44,875
By the way! Did you read the paper?

1073
00:39:44,875 --> 00:39:46,125
It says the Germans again

1074
00:39:46,166 --> 00:39:48,000
sunk a few Allied ships!

1075
00:39:48,166 --> 00:39:50,125
That's all propaganda!

1076
00:39:50,333 --> 00:39:51,083
The Germans,

1077
00:39:51,125 --> 00:39:54,208
if they sink 1000 of these ships too,

1078
00:39:54,333 --> 00:39:56,208
the English will still win!

1079
00:39:56,916 --> 00:39:59,458
At sea, nobody beats the English!

1080
00:39:59,666 --> 00:40:00,708
And in the air,

1081
00:40:00,708 --> 00:40:02,416
with this new radar they invented,

1082
00:40:02,458 --> 00:40:04,083
the Germans are finished!

1083
00:40:04,416 --> 00:40:06,958
The Germans always come out strong at the start of a war!

1084
00:40:07,416 --> 00:40:08,708
In the first war, didn't

1085
00:40:08,750 --> 00:40:10,583
the Germans get near Paris,

1086
00:40:10,625 --> 00:40:12,000
then get flattened?

1087
00:40:12,958 --> 00:40:13,958
I don't know,

1088
00:40:13,958 --> 00:40:16,458
why you take the English's side so much?

1089
00:40:16,750 --> 00:40:18,125
Are they paying you something?

1090
00:40:18,291 --> 00:40:19,916
If you take from the Germans,

1091
00:40:19,958 --> 00:40:21,541
why shouldn't I take from the English?

1092
00:40:21,708 --> 00:40:23,333
Is the pound now worth less than the mark?

1093
00:40:23,375 --> 00:40:24,000
No!

1094
00:40:24,291 --> 00:40:25,125
Who said?

1095
00:40:25,583 --> 00:40:27,041
Good for you!

1096
00:40:27,500 --> 00:40:29,375
So you take a consulting fee!

1097
00:40:29,666 --> 00:40:31,291
The English in every country,

1098
00:40:31,291 --> 00:40:34,000
have a few seasoned politicians like you!

1099
00:40:34,458 --> 00:40:37,208
Without your great big brain,

1100
00:40:37,208 --> 00:40:38,750
who would Churchill consult!

1101
00:40:38,750 --> 00:40:39,666
And you, if you mean it,

1102
00:40:39,666 --> 00:40:40,833
go be Hitler's adviser!

1103
00:40:40,875 --> 00:40:43,125
These cunning wolves, the English...

1104
00:40:43,125 --> 00:40:45,375
Daddy Dust-Ali! Daddy Dust-Ali, help me!

1105
00:40:45,375 --> 00:40:46,958
Mama wants to kill me! What happened? Be calm!-

1106
00:40:47,708 --> 00:40:48,958
Why talk nonsense, girl?

1107
00:40:49,000 --> 00:40:50,166
Where's Mama?

1108
00:40:50,166 --> 00:40:50,500
Where?

1109
00:40:50,541 --> 00:40:51,250
Oh, drop dead!

1110
00:40:52,250 --> 00:40:55,041
May I live to mourn you! Aziz Khanom! What's going on?-

1111
00:40:55,083 --> 00:40:56,375
You aged me, girl! Calm down!-

1112
00:40:56,583 --> 00:40:57,208
Let go of me!

1113
00:40:57,208 --> 00:40:58,250
Don't get me started!

1114
00:40:58,291 --> 00:40:59,500
Move, let's go home,

1115
00:40:59,541 --> 00:41:01,166
before I smash something on your head! What? Huh?-

1116
00:41:01,208 --> 00:41:02,500
Hurry up! What is it?-

1117
00:41:02,500 --> 00:41:04,166
What happened? What's wrong? Come on, let's go! I'm not coming home...-

1118
00:41:04,208 --> 00:41:05,125
You're not coming home?

1119
00:41:05,125 --> 00:41:07,083
Then see how I drag you!

1120
00:41:07,083 --> 00:41:10,416
You've gone mad! Khanom Aziz-os-Saltaneh, quiet!-

1121
00:41:10,791 --> 00:41:13,916
Sir you don't know what pain I have!

1122
00:41:13,958 --> 00:41:15,291
Let me take her...

1123
00:41:15,291 --> 00:41:16,125
Qamar!

1124
00:41:16,166 --> 00:41:17,916
Go home with Mama.

1125
00:41:18,125 --> 00:41:19,625
I'll tell her to leave you alone.

1126
00:41:19,666 --> 00:41:20,833
I give you my word. Go on, dear.

1127
00:41:21,125 --> 00:41:22,083
Go already!

1128
00:41:22,541 --> 00:41:24,375
I'm not going, I'm afraid!

1129
00:41:24,958 --> 00:41:27,291
Girl, I said go home with Mama!

1130
00:41:27,833 --> 00:41:29,041
I won't go, I won't go!

1131
00:41:29,083 --> 00:41:30,875
I said go home!

1132
00:41:30,875 --> 00:41:32,916
Don't talk back!

1133
00:41:32,916 --> 00:41:33,625
I won't go!

1134
00:41:33,875 --> 00:41:36,125
Mama wants to kill my child!

1135
00:41:36,166 --> 00:41:37,125
I love him!

1136
00:41:37,125 --> 00:41:39,875
I want to knit him a red blouse.

1137
00:41:39,916 --> 00:41:40,833
What? A child?

1138
00:41:41,875 --> 00:41:42,416
Meaning what?

1139
00:41:42,458 --> 00:41:44,000
A blouse? What did Qamar say?!

1140
00:41:44,083 --> 00:41:45,958
Huh? A child?!

1141
00:41:47,166 --> 00:41:48,875
God, let me die

1142
00:41:48,916 --> 00:41:51,875
so I won't bear this shame!

1143
00:41:51,958 --> 00:41:52,875
But...!

1144
00:41:56,541 --> 00:41:57,250
You...

1145
00:41:58,375 --> 00:41:59,333
A child...

1146
00:42:00,375 --> 00:42:01,166
You...

1147
00:42:03,333 --> 00:42:07,333
You still... don't know... the English!

1148
00:42:07,333 --> 00:42:08,625
Sir! Sir!

1149
00:42:08,708 --> 00:42:09,875
Sir! Sir! He's taken ill!-

1150
00:42:12,541 --> 00:42:13,333
Sir, please!

1151
00:42:14,708 --> 00:42:15,958
Sit! Sit!

1152
00:42:17,083 --> 00:42:17,875
Easy!

1153
00:42:18,333 --> 00:42:19,000
Water!

1154
00:42:19,041 --> 00:42:20,416
Bring water for him!

1155
00:42:20,416 --> 00:42:21,291
Baba-jun!

1156
00:42:21,333 --> 00:42:24,541
They'll be the death of my father! Sir's heart has seized! Water won't help!-

1157
00:42:24,833 --> 00:42:26,916
Send for Doctor Naser-ol-Hokama!

1158
00:42:27,541 --> 00:42:28,833
No! No! Be calm!-

1159
00:42:29,250 --> 00:42:32,375
A doctor isn't needed!

1160
00:42:32,375 --> 00:42:34,375
That doctor,

1161
00:42:34,375 --> 00:42:41,250
his nephew works for the English oil company!

1162
00:42:41,750 --> 00:42:42,458
Saeed!

1163
00:42:42,458 --> 00:42:43,791
Leili! Kids, out!-

1164
00:42:43,833 --> 00:42:45,208
Please go play in that room.

1165
00:42:45,250 --> 00:42:46,000
Go out!

1166
00:42:46,041 --> 00:42:46,500
Moment!

1167
00:42:46,541 --> 00:42:47,416
Mister Colonel!

1168
00:42:47,416 --> 00:42:49,125
There are no small kids here!

1169
00:42:49,166 --> 00:42:49,916
They're big!

1170
00:42:49,916 --> 00:42:51,708
Besides, they've heard it all!

1171
00:42:51,750 --> 00:42:53,041
You, mister Colonel,

1172
00:42:53,083 --> 00:42:54,666
if you don't want this scandal to get out,

1173
00:42:54,666 --> 00:42:55,625
you'd better let them stay!

1174
00:42:55,666 --> 00:42:57,250
But kids! Don't tell anyone, you hear!

1175
00:42:57,250 --> 00:42:58,625
At your age,

1176
00:42:58,666 --> 00:43:00,208
with your weak heart,

1177
00:43:00,291 --> 00:43:03,291
too much excitement could cost you your life!

1178
00:43:03,291 --> 00:43:03,666
Yes!

1179
00:43:03,708 --> 00:43:05,708
You're right!

1180
00:43:07,000 --> 00:43:11,166
In such a position,

1181
00:43:11,375 --> 00:43:16,333
We mustn't panic!

1182
00:43:17,208 --> 00:43:18,333
Kids!

1183
00:43:18,375 --> 00:43:19,541
Kids! Yes yes!-

1184
00:43:20,125 --> 00:43:22,375
Take them out! Leili-jun! You wait outside. Saeed, you go out too!

1185
00:43:22,416 --> 00:43:24,000
Out! Wait outside a minute! In that room.

1186
00:43:24,000 --> 00:43:25,125
Go, go! Go!

1187
00:43:25,666 --> 00:43:27,416
My daddy isn't well! He's fine, go!-

1188
00:43:27,458 --> 00:43:28,375
Wait in the yard.

1189
00:43:28,416 --> 00:43:29,083
Go, go!

1190
00:43:29,166 --> 00:43:31,166
♪ Sad music ♪

1191
00:43:43,125 --> 00:43:44,333
I wanted to ask,

1192
00:43:44,791 --> 00:43:46,583
if Puri comes back, will you become his wife?

1193
00:43:46,791 --> 00:43:47,541
I don't know!

1194
00:43:47,750 --> 00:43:48,916
If they force you?

1195
00:43:49,541 --> 00:43:50,708
I'll kill myself

1196
00:43:54,000 --> 00:43:54,500
Leili!

1197
00:43:55,666 --> 00:43:56,250
Leili!

1198
00:43:58,666 --> 00:43:59,250
Come!

1199
00:43:59,250 --> 00:44:00,916
I wrote this letter for you last night.

1200
00:44:02,958 --> 00:44:05,541
There are things I'd never dare say to you.

1201
00:44:11,500 --> 00:44:12,458
Qamar-jun!

1202
00:44:12,583 --> 00:44:13,791
Tell your uncle.

1203
00:44:14,000 --> 00:44:16,875
But how do you know you're having a baby?

1204
00:44:16,916 --> 00:44:18,958
He moves inside my tummy!

1205
00:44:19,208 --> 00:44:20,583
Since when have you known?

1206
00:44:20,791 --> 00:44:22,458
From a few days ago!

1207
00:44:22,791 --> 00:44:25,166
I took the money out of my piggy bank,

1208
00:44:25,166 --> 00:44:26,875
I bought red yarn,

1209
00:44:26,916 --> 00:44:28,708
to knit him a blouse!

1210
00:44:28,791 --> 00:44:29,500
Look!

1211
00:44:29,750 --> 00:44:30,916
Qamar-jun!

1212
00:44:31,000 --> 00:44:35,541
But a girl can't have a baby until she gets married!

1213
00:44:35,541 --> 00:44:38,708
When did you get married without us knowing?!

1214
00:44:38,958 --> 00:44:41,333
I got married at the start of summer!

1215
00:44:41,416 --> 00:44:42,541
Oh? Mm-hm!-

1216
00:44:42,625 --> 00:44:43,791
What was his name?

1217
00:44:44,000 --> 00:44:45,500
Do you know now where he is?

1218
00:44:45,541 --> 00:44:47,125
Mm-hm! Mm-hm!

1219
00:44:47,208 --> 00:44:48,500
But I won't say!

1220
00:44:49,125 --> 00:44:51,916
Whisper it to your uncle!

1221
00:44:52,291 --> 00:44:54,250
Sir, we tried and tried,

1222
00:44:54,250 --> 00:44:56,166
she wouldn't say the man's name!

1223
00:44:56,500 --> 00:44:57,791
Think again!

1224
00:44:57,833 --> 00:44:59,416
Don't tire yourselves for nothing!

1225
00:44:59,625 --> 00:45:03,416
Well, she didn't tell you! She'll tell me.

1226
00:45:03,500 --> 00:45:04,750
Isn't that so uncle-jun? No!-

1227
00:45:04,750 --> 00:45:05,500
I won't say!

1228
00:45:05,541 --> 00:45:08,125
(Hubbub of the gathering)

1229
00:45:08,166 --> 00:45:09,458
You must say!

1230
00:45:09,541 --> 00:45:11,625
You must say!

1231
00:45:11,666 --> 00:45:13,208
Speak!

1232
00:45:13,333 --> 00:45:14,833
I'll kill you!

1233
00:45:14,875 --> 00:45:16,708
You must say! I don't want to say!-

1234
00:45:16,708 --> 00:45:19,125
You must say! I don't want to say! I don't want!-

1235
00:45:19,125 --> 00:45:21,166
Sir! Sir!

1236
00:45:21,208 --> 00:45:24,000
Poor thing! Stop tormenting her! If I tell, you'll kill my baby!-

1237
00:45:24,166 --> 00:45:27,583
Don't interfere! It's none of your business!

1238
00:45:27,583 --> 00:45:29,625
Sir, this girl isn't all there!

1239
00:45:29,666 --> 00:45:30,791
She's cracked!

1240
00:45:30,833 --> 00:45:31,416
What did you say?

1241
00:45:31,458 --> 00:45:33,291
Do you know what you're saying or not?

1242
00:45:33,291 --> 00:45:35,208
You're the one not all there!

1243
00:45:35,250 --> 00:45:37,291
Are you saying my daughter is crazy?

1244
00:45:38,250 --> 00:45:40,708
May you burn in hell, girl, -Moment!

1245
00:45:40,708 --> 00:45:43,000
for making me the talk of the family! Don't shout!-

1246
00:45:43,000 --> 00:45:45,083
Let go of me Asdollah! Don't you see what she's saying!

1247
00:45:45,666 --> 00:45:47,666
Leave her, Aziz Khanom!-

1248
00:45:47,666 --> 00:45:49,041
How can I be calm! Calm down!-

1249
00:45:49,083 --> 00:45:50,916
She's saying my daughter is mad!

1250
00:45:51,375 --> 00:45:54,500
(Shouting and yelling)

1251
00:45:54,916 --> 00:45:56,250
Calm her, Asdollah!

1252
00:45:57,916 --> 00:45:59,375
Don't cry my dear!

1253
00:45:59,458 --> 00:46:02,000
No one can kill your baby!

1254
00:46:02,208 --> 00:46:03,833
A child that has a father,

1255
00:46:03,875 --> 00:46:06,083
no one can kill him!

1256
00:46:06,666 --> 00:46:07,875
If Sir asks

1257
00:46:07,958 --> 00:46:09,291
who the baby's father is,

1258
00:46:09,291 --> 00:46:11,041
it's so they can find him and bring him here

1259
00:46:11,041 --> 00:46:13,458
to live with wife and child.

1260
00:46:13,500 --> 00:46:14,083
Meaning,

1261
00:46:14,125 --> 00:46:15,333
you and your child!

1262
00:46:15,333 --> 00:46:17,625
But he isn't here!

1263
00:46:17,625 --> 00:46:18,458
Where is he?

1264
00:46:19,625 --> 00:46:20,708
Leave her!

1265
00:46:20,708 --> 00:46:22,375
This girl will never say anything! Enough!-

1266
00:46:22,416 --> 00:46:25,583
We questioned her all night till morning, she didn't say a word!

1267
00:46:27,125 --> 00:46:29,041
Churchill's special adviser, shut up!

1268
00:46:29,250 --> 00:46:31,000
Shut up, you Hitler-lover!

1269
00:46:31,500 --> 00:46:33,583
Even Goebbels can't match you!

1270
00:46:33,916 --> 00:46:35,833
What does this have to do with you anyway?

1271
00:46:36,208 --> 00:46:37,833
Don't tell me it's propaganda?

1272
00:46:37,833 --> 00:46:38,875
Shut up already!

1273
00:46:38,875 --> 00:46:41,000
If not out of respect for Sir,

1274
00:46:41,041 --> 00:46:42,208
I'd hit you over the head so hard

1275
00:46:42,208 --> 00:46:44,041
your brains would spill out your nose!

1276
00:46:44,041 --> 00:46:46,458
Sir, someone put this jackass Dust-Ali in his place!

1277
00:46:46,541 --> 00:46:47,541
What's wrong,

1278
00:46:47,541 --> 00:46:49,958
fighting like cats and dogs?

1279
00:46:50,000 --> 00:46:51,333
Sit down, Dust-Ali!

1280
00:46:54,541 --> 00:46:55,458
My dear!

1281
00:46:56,458 --> 00:46:58,416
If you say where your husband is,

1282
00:46:58,458 --> 00:47:00,791
maybe we can find him!

1283
00:47:01,291 --> 00:47:04,708
If I tell you, do you promise not to kill my baby? Huh?

1284
00:47:04,750 --> 00:47:06,625
I knitted him a blouse!

1285
00:47:06,791 --> 00:47:08,708
Only its sleeves are left.

1286
00:47:08,833 --> 00:47:10,333
I promise my dear.

1287
00:47:10,375 --> 00:47:10,875
Come.

1288
00:47:11,416 --> 00:47:13,333
Come have a sweet.

1289
00:47:16,875 --> 00:47:18,958
His name is Allah-Verdi.

1290
00:47:19,000 --> 00:47:19,416
Huh?

1291
00:47:19,791 --> 00:47:20,833
Allah...

1292
00:47:21,333 --> 00:47:22,583
Allah-Verdi!

1293
00:47:22,875 --> 00:47:24,416
Which Allah-Verdi?

1294
00:47:24,416 --> 00:47:26,250
Allah-Verdi, I said!

1295
00:47:29,250 --> 00:47:31,833
Don't tell me Allah-Verdi is this Indian fellow's servant?!

1296
00:47:32,041 --> 00:47:33,958
The Sardar has no servant!

1297
00:47:34,166 --> 00:47:37,250
He did! Before, when he lived in that tree alley,

1298
00:47:37,416 --> 00:47:39,500
he had a servant named Allah-Verdi.

1299
00:47:40,041 --> 00:47:42,166
He stole from the Sardar's pocket, so he threw him out.

1300
00:47:42,208 --> 00:47:44,875
See, I said this is the English's plan!

1301
00:47:45,041 --> 00:47:47,916
By attacking our family's honor,

1302
00:47:47,916 --> 00:47:48,625
they've set out.

1303
00:47:48,625 --> 00:47:50,875
Why don't you people understand?

1304
00:47:50,916 --> 00:47:53,708
Sir! Getting so worked up is bad for your heart!

1305
00:47:53,750 --> 00:47:54,333
Permit...

1306
00:47:54,375 --> 00:47:55,833
God damn you, girl!

1307
00:47:55,875 --> 00:47:58,166
Girl, I hope I live to mourn you!

1308
00:47:58,208 --> 00:48:00,833
I pray to the Holy Five they bring me news of your death!

1309
00:48:00,958 --> 00:48:02,041
Shame on you,

1310
00:48:02,041 --> 00:48:03,458
with an Indian servant?

1311
00:48:03,458 --> 00:48:05,583
God, let me die!

1312
00:48:07,041 --> 00:48:08,958
The Indian Sardar's servant!

1313
00:48:09,000 --> 00:48:11,125
Clearly I'm the target!

1314
00:48:11,125 --> 00:48:14,416
I and my family must be destroyed!

1315
00:48:14,458 --> 00:48:15,916
No doubt this is the English's work too!

1316
00:48:16,583 --> 00:48:17,750
Wretched English!

1317
00:48:17,791 --> 00:48:18,625
You!

1318
00:48:20,000 --> 00:48:22,583
You take their side too?

1319
00:48:22,583 --> 00:48:23,791
You!

1320
00:48:23,791 --> 00:48:25,500
My own cousin!

1321
00:48:25,625 --> 00:48:27,625
I, I, I, I said nothing, Sir!

1322
00:48:27,666 --> 00:48:29,083
I did nothing!

1323
00:48:30,083 --> 00:48:33,083
Forgive him, Sir! This man has no sense!

1324
00:48:33,625 --> 00:48:35,375
And now is not the time for this talk!

1325
00:48:35,583 --> 00:48:37,208
Whenever a man wants to speak,

1326
00:48:37,208 --> 00:48:38,083
they say it's not the time!

1327
00:48:38,125 --> 00:48:40,166
Why isn't it the time for this?

1328
00:48:40,291 --> 00:48:41,041
Asdollah!

1329
00:48:41,041 --> 00:48:42,541
You don't understand!

1330
00:48:42,541 --> 00:48:45,916
There are some things that you don't know!

1331
00:48:46,000 --> 00:48:48,541
And you still kid yourself that you work for the Foreign Ministry!

1332
00:48:48,708 --> 00:48:50,166
Don't be angry, Sir!

1333
00:48:50,166 --> 00:48:52,083
Suppose it is their politics!

1334
00:48:52,166 --> 00:48:53,958
Let us get to the bottom of it!

1335
00:48:54,166 --> 00:48:57,416
Politics is far too complicated

1336
00:48:57,416 --> 00:49:00,291
for just anyone to get!

1337
00:49:00,625 --> 00:49:01,458
Tell me, Qamar!

1338
00:49:02,083 --> 00:49:05,000
Who is this Allah-Verdi? Where is he?

1339
00:49:05,333 --> 00:49:06,708
I don't want to say!

1340
00:49:07,125 --> 00:49:09,208
Asdollah Sir is right!

1341
00:49:09,250 --> 00:49:10,291
Before anything,

1342
00:49:10,333 --> 00:49:12,958
we must think of finding Allah-Verdi.

1343
00:49:13,041 --> 00:49:15,625
Find Allah-Verdi and do what?

1344
00:49:15,750 --> 00:49:17,666
My respected cousin,

1345
00:49:17,833 --> 00:49:20,041
to Allah-Verdi, this Indian's servant,

1346
00:49:20,083 --> 00:49:21,375
you'd marry her off?

1347
00:49:21,416 --> 00:49:23,625
Sir, if you can think of another way,

1348
00:49:23,666 --> 00:49:24,333
tell us!

1349
00:49:24,375 --> 00:49:26,500
Please, don't you interfere!

1350
00:49:26,666 --> 00:49:28,333
The dignity of an aristocratic family

1351
00:49:28,333 --> 00:49:30,500
isn't something you can grasp!

1352
00:49:30,875 --> 00:49:31,375
Where?

1353
00:49:31,416 --> 00:49:32,500
Let your servant leave!

1354
00:49:32,541 --> 00:49:34,291
Please, stay.

1355
00:49:34,708 --> 00:49:37,125
So you married Allah-Verdi!

1356
00:49:38,208 --> 00:49:38,666
Well!

1357
00:49:39,333 --> 00:49:41,625
I bet one day when you were home alone,

1358
00:49:41,625 --> 00:49:42,166
he came, said:

1359
00:49:42,166 --> 00:49:44,000
Qamar-jun, I love you.

1360
00:49:44,041 --> 00:49:45,166
Let's get married.

1361
00:49:45,208 --> 00:49:45,958
Right?

1362
00:49:46,375 --> 00:49:47,083
No!

1363
00:49:47,666 --> 00:49:48,875
Well then one day,

1364
00:49:48,916 --> 00:49:50,416
when his master wasn't home,

1365
00:49:50,500 --> 00:49:51,875
he told you,

1366
00:49:52,166 --> 00:49:53,625
let's marry at our place!

1367
00:49:53,958 --> 00:49:54,708
Yes, sweetie?

1368
00:49:55,166 --> 00:49:56,000
No!

1369
00:49:56,000 --> 00:49:56,458
Well!

1370
00:49:57,416 --> 00:49:59,500
I bet one day when you were in the alley,

1371
00:49:59,500 --> 00:50:00,750
he told you,

1372
00:50:00,791 --> 00:50:02,416
let's go to a friend's house and marry.

1373
00:50:02,416 --> 00:50:03,375
Right, Qamar-jun?

1374
00:50:03,458 --> 00:50:05,541
No! It wasn't the alley!

1375
00:50:08,541 --> 00:50:10,875
What shameless people exist!

1376
00:50:11,416 --> 00:50:14,375
A cookie now, Uncle Asdollah? You're always thinking of your stomach!-

1377
00:50:18,375 --> 00:50:18,916
Come!

1378
00:50:21,458 --> 00:50:22,833
So Allah-Verdi,

1379
00:50:23,375 --> 00:50:25,208
came on your rooftop, yes?

1380
00:50:25,333 --> 00:50:25,875
No!

1381
00:50:25,916 --> 00:50:27,125
He didn't come! Not at all!-

1382
00:50:27,250 --> 00:50:28,333
Didn't I say?

1383
00:50:28,583 --> 00:50:29,833
You can't get

1384
00:50:29,833 --> 00:50:32,000
a straight word out of this girl!

1385
00:50:32,125 --> 00:50:33,791
Don't torment yourselves for nothing!

1386
00:50:34,125 --> 00:50:35,750
I know it's no use.

1387
00:50:35,750 --> 00:50:38,000
We've been at it for days, and nothing!

1388
00:50:38,083 --> 00:50:39,916
Think of something else!

1389
00:50:40,083 --> 00:50:42,416
These few days have worn me out!

1390
00:50:42,500 --> 00:50:44,375
Let Asdollah ask her!

1391
00:50:44,375 --> 00:50:45,750
Want to stay up tonight like last night,

1392
00:50:45,791 --> 00:50:46,750
till morning?

1393
00:50:46,791 --> 00:50:48,291
Oh, come on, you're dreaming!

1394
00:50:50,416 --> 00:50:51,833
Dadash Shams-Ali!

1395
00:50:52,333 --> 00:50:53,250
What is it dadash?

1396
00:50:53,500 --> 00:50:54,208
I think,

1397
00:50:54,250 --> 00:50:57,750
The Holy Spirit went to San Francisco with Qamar once too!

1398
00:50:57,791 --> 00:50:59,791
(Laughter of the gathering)

1399
00:51:03,958 --> 00:51:05,041
Uncle Asdollah?

1400
00:51:05,083 --> 00:51:07,416
Remember you said if I was a good girl,

1401
00:51:07,416 --> 00:51:09,208
you'll take me to San Francisco?

1402
00:51:09,208 --> 00:51:10,666
So why didn't you? Huh?

1403
00:51:10,708 --> 00:51:11,750
Who knows Qamar-jun?

1404
00:51:11,916 --> 00:51:13,000
Who knows?

1405
00:51:13,666 --> 00:51:14,708
Maybe this souvenir

1406
00:51:14,708 --> 00:51:17,541
Uncle Asdollah brought you from San Francisco!

1407
00:51:17,541 --> 00:51:18,083
Shut up!

1408
00:51:18,125 --> 00:51:20,291
Eh! Dadash! Dadash!

1409
00:51:20,541 --> 00:51:21,916
Dadash! Be calm!

1410
00:51:22,041 --> 00:51:23,208
Leave him!

1411
00:51:23,750 --> 00:51:24,291
Go!

1412
00:51:24,708 --> 00:51:25,458
Go sit.

1413
00:51:27,166 --> 00:51:29,708
Hey Dust-Ali! What the hell?

1414
00:51:30,250 --> 00:51:31,458
Sit down!

1415
00:51:31,916 --> 00:51:32,375
Well!

1416
00:51:33,125 --> 00:51:34,833
So Allah-Verdi didn't come to your house,

1417
00:51:34,833 --> 00:51:36,291
or take you to his house,

1418
00:51:36,291 --> 00:51:38,375
or the little bazaar, or up on the rooftop!

1419
00:51:38,500 --> 00:51:39,791
Then where?

1420
00:51:40,750 --> 00:51:42,208
Who came?

1421
00:51:43,250 --> 00:51:44,833
Aha!

1422
00:51:45,000 --> 00:51:47,833
Maybe in the car?

1423
00:51:48,833 --> 00:51:49,333
No!

1424
00:51:49,333 --> 00:51:51,458
An Indian servant with a car?!

1425
00:51:52,166 --> 00:51:53,666
Then how?

1426
00:51:54,208 --> 00:51:55,791
Where did you even see Allah-Verdi?

1427
00:51:56,083 --> 00:51:57,666
I didn't see him!

1428
00:51:58,083 --> 00:51:58,541
You didn't?

1429
00:51:58,625 --> 00:52:00,875
No, I swear! I didn't!

1430
00:52:01,166 --> 00:52:02,583
Then it's very strange!

1431
00:52:02,583 --> 00:52:04,625
So you went to San Francisco unseen?

1432
00:52:06,083 --> 00:52:07,125
Qamar-jun?

1433
00:52:07,166 --> 00:52:08,958
You even know Allah-Verdi? No!-

1434
00:52:09,375 --> 00:52:10,166
No!

1435
00:52:10,208 --> 00:52:10,916
Moment!

1436
00:52:11,041 --> 00:52:13,041
Truly Moment!

1437
00:52:13,250 --> 00:52:15,625
Then how is Allah-Verdi your baby's father?

1438
00:52:16,000 --> 00:52:18,208
How do you know he's your baby's father?

1439
00:52:18,541 --> 00:52:19,666
Daddy Dust-Ali said

1440
00:52:19,708 --> 00:52:22,083
my baby's father is Allah-Verdi!

1441
00:52:22,208 --> 00:52:23,250
I, I, I!-

1442
00:52:23,666 --> 00:52:24,458
Meaning what!-

1443
00:52:24,500 --> 00:52:25,750
L...l...l...lie!-

1444
00:52:25,750 --> 00:52:26,458
Dust-Ali?!

1445
00:52:26,500 --> 00:52:27,916
L...l...l...lie!-

1446
00:52:28,250 --> 00:52:30,250
God is witness I...

1447
00:52:30,500 --> 00:52:31,625
I...I...I...

1448
00:52:32,333 --> 00:52:34,291
This girl is mad!

1449
00:52:34,416 --> 00:52:35,958
Her brain is defective!

1450
00:52:36,000 --> 00:52:38,041
By God her brain is defective!

1451
00:52:38,083 --> 00:52:38,708
I!

1452
00:52:38,791 --> 00:52:39,416
I!

1453
00:52:39,416 --> 00:52:43,583
(He falls into a stutter)

1454
00:52:43,666 --> 00:52:44,250
By the soul...

1455
00:52:44,291 --> 00:52:46,250
By the soul of Great Sir I swear!

1456
00:52:46,541 --> 00:52:48,208
She's accusing me!

1457
00:52:48,250 --> 00:52:49,416
I... by the soul...

1458
00:52:49,416 --> 00:52:51,666
I swear on my father's soul, I know nothing!

1459
00:52:51,708 --> 00:52:53,666
I don't know anything! Spit it out! Why did you say this?-

1460
00:52:53,666 --> 00:52:55,416
Why did you tell Qamar to say this?

1461
00:52:55,583 --> 00:52:58,125
Why did you tell Qamar to say it was Allah-Verdi? Why?

1462
00:52:58,541 --> 00:53:00,833
Talk, man! Why have you gone silent? Say it!

1463
00:53:01,375 --> 00:53:01,958
Say!

1464
00:53:02,000 --> 00:53:03,125
I... I... because,

1465
00:53:03,166 --> 00:53:04,875
I saw she didn't know the man's name,

1466
00:53:04,916 --> 00:53:07,333
I swear I just wanted to avoid a scandal!

1467
00:53:07,875 --> 00:53:08,708
I'll kill you!

1468
00:53:08,708 --> 00:53:09,875
Mama! Mama!

1469
00:53:09,958 --> 00:53:11,625
Daddy Dust-Ali tells so many lies!

1470
00:53:11,625 --> 00:53:13,916
Didn't you say, if you don't say Allah-Verdi is the father,

1471
00:53:13,958 --> 00:53:15,208
I'll kill your baby?

1472
00:53:15,375 --> 00:53:16,375
I said?

1473
00:53:16,791 --> 00:53:17,625
I said?

1474
00:53:18,041 --> 00:53:18,958
I said?

1475
00:53:19,041 --> 00:53:21,500
Believe me! I swear to God I'm innocent!

1476
00:53:21,500 --> 00:53:22,750
Who'd believe it?

1477
00:53:22,791 --> 00:53:25,333
Me with my own stepdaughter?!

1478
00:53:25,833 --> 00:53:27,458
Who'd believe that?

1479
00:53:27,833 --> 00:53:29,458
Sir, say something!

1480
00:53:29,500 --> 00:53:31,000
But how is it possible!

1481
00:53:32,791 --> 00:53:34,916
Then tell the truth, or I'll riddle you with holes!

1482
00:53:34,958 --> 00:53:36,083
Khanom Aziz-os-Saltaneh!

1483
00:53:36,416 --> 00:53:39,583
Careful! That rifle is loaded! Don't move!-

1484
00:53:39,666 --> 00:53:40,666
Don't move!

1485
00:53:40,958 --> 00:53:41,375
Aziz-junam!

1486
00:53:41,375 --> 00:53:42,333
Stay where you are!

1487
00:53:42,625 --> 00:53:44,583
Aziz Khanom!

1488
00:53:44,625 --> 00:53:47,208
On Leili's life, that rifle is loaded!

1489
00:53:47,250 --> 00:53:48,458
I loaded it

1490
00:53:48,500 --> 00:53:50,041
so if the English army arrived,

1491
00:53:50,041 --> 00:53:51,125
we wouldn't be surprised!

1492
00:53:51,125 --> 00:53:51,875
Everyone back!

1493
00:53:52,000 --> 00:53:53,708
Everyone sit down and shut up!

1494
00:53:53,750 --> 00:53:54,625
Aziz-junam!

1495
00:53:54,708 --> 00:53:55,000
I!

1496
00:53:55,250 --> 00:53:56,958
Dishonorable coward!

1497
00:53:57,166 --> 00:53:59,000
Talk! Talk, you wretch!

1498
00:53:59,041 --> 00:54:01,416
Why did you tell Qamar to say it was Allah-Verdi? Talk!

1499
00:54:01,541 --> 00:54:02,250
Say!

1500
00:54:02,333 --> 00:54:03,208
By God!

1501
00:54:03,208 --> 00:54:04,958
On my mother's soul, I didn't!

1502
00:54:04,958 --> 00:54:06,875
And if I did, I meant no harm! Aziz Khanom!-

1503
00:54:06,916 --> 00:54:08,875
I just wanted to avoid a scandal!

1504
00:54:09,208 --> 00:54:10,625
Don't waste a bullet on him! Aziz-junam!-

1505
00:54:10,833 --> 00:54:11,666
Give me the rifle!

1506
00:54:11,750 --> 00:54:13,916
Aziz-jun... give... let go... give it!

1507
00:54:13,916 --> 00:54:14,833
Let go of me Asdollah!

1508
00:54:14,875 --> 00:54:15,250
Run!

1509
00:54:16,666 --> 00:54:17,500
Go on, man!

1510
00:54:17,541 --> 00:54:19,625
Run while she's distracted! Run!

1511
00:54:19,916 --> 00:54:20,958
The rifle! Eh, eh, eh!

1512
00:54:21,000 --> 00:54:21,916
Oh, Saint Abbas!-

1513
00:54:21,958 --> 00:54:22,625
Stop, you wretch!

1514
00:54:22,666 --> 00:54:23,791
Stop! Hold him!-

1515
00:54:23,791 --> 00:54:25,125
(Sound of the telephone ringing)

1516
00:54:25,166 --> 00:54:26,416
Asdollah! Hold him! Grab him!

1517
00:54:26,458 --> 00:54:27,041
Yes? Asdollah!-

1518
00:54:27,041 --> 00:54:27,791
I'll rip you apart!

1519
00:54:27,791 --> 00:54:29,250
It's for you! I'm not here! Say I'm not here!-

1520
00:54:29,291 --> 00:54:29,916
He's not here!

1521
00:54:29,958 --> 00:54:31,000
(Hubbub of the gathering)

1522
00:54:31,000 --> 00:54:32,791
Don't shoot! For God's sake!

1523
00:54:32,791 --> 00:54:33,708
Don't!

1524
00:54:33,750 --> 00:54:34,583
(Sound of a rifle shot)

1525
00:54:34,875 --> 00:54:37,458
(Sound of Dust-Ali’s scream and the gathering’s hubbub)

1526
00:54:40,416 --> 00:54:41,291
Blood!

1527
00:54:41,333 --> 00:54:42,125
Dust-Ali!

1528
00:54:42,125 --> 00:54:42,958
Dust-Ali!

1529
00:54:42,958 --> 00:54:44,291
Dust-Ali what happened?!

1530
00:54:44,333 --> 00:54:45,708
Come help!

1531
00:54:45,708 --> 00:54:46,666
Where did it hit him?

1532
00:54:46,666 --> 00:54:47,416
Dust-Ali!

1533
00:54:48,791 --> 00:54:51,166
Woman see what you did!

1534
00:54:51,208 --> 00:54:52,291
Where did it hit you? Blood!-

1535
00:54:52,291 --> 00:54:53,833
Where did it hit you? It's burning!-

1536
00:54:53,875 --> 00:54:54,875
Mama, mama!

1537
00:54:54,875 --> 00:54:56,208
Did you kill him or not?

1538
00:54:56,208 --> 00:54:58,583
Well done, Mama!

1539
00:54:59,000 --> 00:55:01,000
Mama dear! You did a good thing,

1540
00:55:01,041 --> 00:55:02,458
you killed Dad Dust-Ali!

1541
00:55:02,875 --> 00:55:06,166
Remember he kept saying go to the doctor, get rid of the baby?

1542
00:55:06,166 --> 00:55:06,958
Oh! Stop it, girl!

1543
00:55:06,958 --> 00:55:08,083
Serves him right!

1544
00:55:08,125 --> 00:55:11,333
Now he can't kill my baby, right?

1545
00:55:12,041 --> 00:55:12,958
Dust-Ali!

1546
00:55:13,000 --> 00:55:13,541
Dust-Ali!

1547
00:55:13,583 --> 00:55:14,791
At least let me see what happened!

1548
00:55:14,833 --> 00:55:15,500
Blood!

1549
00:55:15,708 --> 00:55:17,708
(Dust-Ali cries out)

1550
00:55:17,750 --> 00:55:18,416
Easy now!-

1551
00:55:19,250 --> 00:55:20,291
Very well!

1552
00:55:20,333 --> 00:55:21,541
Very well!

1553
00:55:22,750 --> 00:55:23,416
Let me see what happened!

1554
00:55:23,458 --> 00:55:24,083
I'm dead, doc!

1555
00:55:24,125 --> 00:55:26,625
Let me see where it hit you, man!

1556
00:55:26,666 --> 00:55:28,375
My butt, my butt!

1557
00:55:28,375 --> 00:55:30,125
Oh no! Where did it hit him?-

1558
00:55:30,166 --> 00:55:30,958
Nothing!

1559
00:55:31,000 --> 00:55:32,875
This was a blister, now it burst!

1560
00:55:32,916 --> 00:55:36,125
Asdollah, shame on you! Enough joking!

1561
00:55:36,375 --> 00:55:37,291
Moment!

1562
00:55:37,333 --> 00:55:39,625
He won't be sitting on that seat again!

1563
00:55:39,875 --> 00:55:41,291
(Dust-Ali moans)

1564
00:55:41,291 --> 00:55:42,833
Don't move, it gets worse!

1565
00:55:42,833 --> 00:55:45,083
Sir-jun, Sir-jun! What happened? What happened?

1566
00:55:45,125 --> 00:55:45,750
It's nothing!

1567
00:55:46,500 --> 00:55:48,250
I'm dying!

1568
00:55:48,750 --> 00:55:49,958
Uncle Asdollah what happened?

1569
00:55:50,208 --> 00:55:50,791
Huh?

1570
00:55:50,791 --> 00:55:51,541
What happened?

1571
00:55:51,583 --> 00:55:52,291
Nothing!

1572
00:55:52,333 --> 00:55:54,791
The poor devil, for one trip to San Francisco,

1573
00:55:54,833 --> 00:55:56,833
must sleep face-down for life!

1574
00:55:56,875 --> 00:55:57,500
But why?

1575
00:55:57,541 --> 00:55:58,875
His darling Aziz shot him!

1576
00:55:58,916 --> 00:55:59,750
Aziz Khanom?!

1577
00:56:00,416 --> 00:56:01,916
Let me see, man! Let me see!

1578
00:56:01,916 --> 00:56:03,083
Ay, ay, ay, ay!

1579
00:56:03,791 --> 00:56:05,958
He's torn to shreds!

1580
00:56:05,958 --> 00:56:07,541
Moment! Moment!

1581
00:56:07,750 --> 00:56:09,208
He's fooling you!

1582
00:56:09,250 --> 00:56:10,208
He's fine!

1583
00:56:10,666 --> 00:56:11,541
Two little pellets

1584
00:56:11,583 --> 00:56:13,791
that could barely knock a button loose,

1585
00:56:14,208 --> 00:56:16,166
against a ton of jackass Dust-Ali's rump,

1586
00:56:16,166 --> 00:56:17,291
what can they do?

1587
00:56:18,541 --> 00:56:19,583
He's so scared of Aziz Khanom

1588
00:56:19,583 --> 00:56:20,750
he's playing dead!

1589
00:56:20,791 --> 00:56:21,291
Asdollah!-

1590
00:56:22,083 --> 00:56:23,625
Stop it, Asdollah!

1591
00:56:23,625 --> 00:56:25,333
This wretched one is dying!

1592
00:56:25,416 --> 00:56:26,416
Instead of talking,

1593
00:56:26,458 --> 00:56:29,750
help us get him to Doctor Naser-ol-Hokama's house!

1594
00:56:29,791 --> 00:56:31,708
Doctor Naser-ol-Hokama is no use!

1595
00:56:31,708 --> 00:56:33,666
We must get him to the hospital!

1596
00:56:33,708 --> 00:56:35,625
He's right, Colonel! The hospital is better!

1597
00:56:35,666 --> 00:56:36,666
No, no!

1598
00:56:36,708 --> 00:56:38,083
I don't think that's wise!

1599
00:56:38,083 --> 00:56:39,875
Think of something else!

1600
00:56:40,416 --> 00:56:42,291
Forget the hospital!

1601
00:56:42,333 --> 00:56:44,625
It'll become a big affair!

1602
00:56:44,625 --> 00:56:46,958
The family's honor is in danger!

1603
00:56:46,958 --> 00:56:48,500
You're killing him yourselves!

1604
00:56:48,500 --> 00:56:50,291
Quick, to some other hospital!

1605
00:56:50,291 --> 00:56:52,875
Please, don't interfere anymore!

1606
00:56:52,916 --> 00:56:54,333
That's bullying, Sir!

1607
00:56:54,375 --> 00:56:55,125
Dust-Ali!

1608
00:56:55,166 --> 00:56:57,458
Sir, let's take him to a hospital, anywhere! Get me somewhere!-

1609
00:56:57,500 --> 00:56:59,666
No need for you to interfere!

1610
00:56:59,708 --> 00:57:01,000
Your humble servant has no say in this!

1611
00:57:02,500 --> 00:57:03,208
Dear Doctor!

1612
00:57:03,291 --> 00:57:05,291
Mister Doctor! Where are you going?

1613
00:57:05,333 --> 00:57:06,791
It's none of my business!

1614
00:57:06,791 --> 00:57:07,666
Mister Doctor!

1615
00:57:07,833 --> 00:57:09,416
You've become a kid too!

1616
00:57:09,791 --> 00:57:11,250
Don't be scared, Dust-Ali!

1617
00:57:11,375 --> 00:57:13,458
♪ Ride of the valkyrie ♪

